{
  "raw": {
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Digital-Content-and-Social-Media-Creator_JR100348": {
      "title": "Digital Content and Social Media Creator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary                                                                         The Digital Content and Social Media Creator serves as a digital storyteller and brand ambassador for the College, responsible for increasing Le Moyne’s visibility, fostering institutional pride, and engaging a diverse community of prospective and current students, alumni, faculty, staff, and friends. Operating in an energetic, hands-on capacity, the successful candidate will primarily serve as the lead content producer for the College's primary social channels, executing digital campaigns in alignment with overarching departmental strategy. This individual will conceive, shoot, edit, and publish high-impact multimedia content while actively monitoring community interactions and utilizing data-driven insights to optimize reach. This position offers an exciting opportunity for an adaptable, highly creative, and collaborative professional to build on our strong regional reputation and further expand the College's reach. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Content Creation & Storytelling Develops and executes creative content that aligns with designated monthly campaign themes, driving prospective student engagement throughout key stages of the enrollment lifecycle. Plan, script, shoot, edit, and publish high-quality, engaging content across all official, central Le Moyne channels (i.e., Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, X, YouTube) Gather, capture, and synthesize a wide range of digital media (i.e. photography, news links, quotes, event registration, etc.) into cohesive and impactful content tailored for various platforms and audiences. Leverage content for use on the College’s primary website including feature stories, student spotlights, event recaps, and rich media assets—that are fresh, informative, and aligned with marketing goals. Capture daily campus life, academic achievements, student stories, athletics, and special events in real-time. Comfortably collaborate with students, faculty, and staff. Maintain a cohesive visual identity and authentic brand voice that resonates with prospective students, current students, alumni, the local community, and other constituents. Channel & Community Management Manage daily social media publishing schedules and content calendars. Actively monitor channels to cultivate two-way conversation—responding to comments, direct messages, and brand mentions with warmth, enthusiasm, and accuracy. Serve as the eyes and ears of the college online, fostering a positive, safe, and vibrant online community. Coordinates content reviews and approval workflows, ensuring all assets are vetted prior to publishing Cross-Campus Collaboration Partner proactively with departments across campus to amplify major initiatives and campus stories. Help recruit student workers and coordinate student-created content. Serve as a friendly, approachable liaison who builds trust across every department. Analytics & Optimization Translate data insights into actionable strategies to continuously boost engagement and organic reach. Monitor monthly performance recaps and optimize content accordingly. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree is required. 2–4+ years of professional social media management experience Proven ability to manage projects end-to-end—from initial idea to filming, editing, posting, and measuring—without needing a large production team. Enthusiasm, creativity, and optimism. Ability to thrive in a dynamic environment where news happens fast and priorities shift. Highly approachable, friendly, and outgoing. Equally comfortable walking up to students on campus or collaborating with senior administrators. Expert knowledge of native platform tools (TikTok, IG Reels), capcut/short-form video editing apps, Canva, Adobe Creative Cloud, social scheduling/analytics tools (i.e., Sprout Social, Hootsuite, or similar), and basic experience with Content Management Systems (CMS) for web updates (i.e., WordPress, Cascade, or similar). Comfortable appearing on camera, hosting quick Q&As, or leading video interviews when the content calls for it. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $28.00 - $35.00 per hour (This is an hourly position that calculates to $50,960 - $63,700 annually) Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Manresa-Program_JR100349-1": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Manresa Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Coordinator for Manresa Programs will provide the support needed to serve the students participating in the seminar programs, manage logistics of guest speakers visiting campus, maintain budget controls, assist faculty and staff participating in grant-supported programs, and provide administrative support to the program co-directors. The coordinator will work closely with program co-directors to help Manresa reach its goal of focusing and magnifying the preparation of students for purposeful lives of meaningful success promoted by Le Moyne's Jesuit, liberal arts education. The coordinator will serve as the liaison to the Finance department to ensure compliance with existing and future policies and procedures. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Manresa Seminars (50%) Provide administrative support for the Manresa seminars offered each semester. Tasks include, but are not limited to: Provide direct support to mentors (faculty and staff) through meeting coordination and general problem-solving Maintaining and updating seminar and materials Producing the group materials needed for each seminar Coordinating Facilities and Catering for each seminar Coordinate service opportunities with community partners Monitoring and tracking student progress throughout the semester Maintaining and updating the database of student participant data Coordinate program promotion through print and digital media Attend weekly meetings with professional staff Ensure compliance with College & departmental policies regarding computer usage and personal information Compiling assessment data for later analysis Process invoices and facilitate payments with Accounts Payable Monitor expenses and provide budget updates to the co-directors Assist in preparation of yearly budget reports for grant funders (as applicable) Steward stipends to students and mentors through the payment process Other Manresa Programming (40%) Provide administrative support for Manresa programs outside of the seminar series. These programs could change yearly but planned programs include Purposeful Advising (grant program), Regional Conference, Vocational Companions, Manresa Reading Group, visiting speakers and scholars, and Career Treks.  Tasks include, but are not limited to: Producing the group materials needed for each program Scheduling and room reservations for faculty development seminars, workshops, and retreats Coordinating catering for seminars and workshops Steward stipends to faculty and staff through the payment process Assist in compiling assessment materials of Manresa-related programs  Monitor grant expenditures ○   Assist in producing the interim budget reports for continued grant funding Assist in creation of final budget report to funder(s) Coordinating on-site logistics for visiting speakers and other events Securing transportation and lodging as needed Steward stipends/honoraria through the payment process Tasks specific to Career Treks include: Assisting to prepare students for off-site experiences Creating and monitoring application materials for career treks Secure appropriate transportation and lodging When needed, travel with a co-director to assist in program implementation Collaborate with Alumni Relations staff to plan an alumni event in each city Coordinate with alumni volunteers to finalize hosting details Ensuring assessment measures are implemented and compiled Other responsibilities as assigned (10%) The coordinator is expected to assist staff in Career Advising and Development as needed Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Associate's Degree in Business Management or related field required with 1-2 years of relevant experience, Bachelor's Degree preferred  Managing budgets including accounts payable and general maintenance Demonstrated experience working with confidential information (eg. HIPPA or FERPA) Proven ability to coordinate multiple projects and personnel General knowledge of Higher Education administration and structure Thorough knowledge of G-Suite (Docs, Sheets, etc.) and Microsoft Office Demonstrate strong written & oral communication skills Exceptional interpersonal, organizational, and analytical skills Self-motivated, able to conduct oneself in a highly professional and ethical manner Must be willing to work evening hours from 5:30 pm to 9:30 pm and select weekends as needed Additional Information: Pay Range: $20.00 - $24.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Plumber_JR100352": {
      "title": "Plumber",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Plumbing Mechanic is responsible for the repair, maintenance, operation, adjustment and installation of plumbing fixtures, piping, and equipment. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Install, repair, adjust, service and maintain plumbing drains, water and gas, lines, fixtures and equipment. Inspect plumbing systems, components and perform routine maintenance and repairs. Replace defective pipe, by cutting, bending, soldering and threading defective pipe. Open clogged drains with plumber’s snake or other appropriate tools or devices Replace washers and other worn or defective parts of valves, faucets, shower controls and other similar devices. Be familiar with plumbing codes and regulations including as they relate to food service equipment. Be able to work in biological or anatomical laboratories where human/animal bodies or parts may be expected to worker’s view. Repair or replace damaged plumbing fixtures such as sinks, toilets, showers, and bathtubs and/or connect them to supply and waste pipes using gaskets, couplings, flanges, traps and valves and by soldering connections to make joints as required. As required, estimate materials needed and record time and material expended on each work order. Recommend ordering of necessary parts and supplies for maintenance of equipment. Instruct and advise users of proper operation of equipment. Will be required to make emergency repairs at hours other than normal schedule. May direct helpers and other tradesmen in performance of duties. Install additional plumbing components to improve performance or for adaptation of existing systems. Ordering and installation of necessary lighting, outlets, switches (parts and supplies) for dorm maintenance. Perform duties outside classification incidental to the responsibilities of the Physical Plant Department or such duties assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   High School diploma or equivalent required. Minimum of five years full-time experience in the Plumbing trade with apprenticeship training or equivalent on the job training required. Experience with steam, hot water and chilled water systems required. Provides their own hand tools, and knows materials, methods and hazards of trade. Skill in the use of tools of the trade required. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job, including heavy lifting, working from ladders, scaffolding and lifts required. Must possess a valid NYS Driver’s license. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range:  $26.59 - $28.59 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Student-Health-Services_JR100342": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Health Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   This position provides daily clerical and administrative support to the personnel in the Wellness Center for Health and Counseling.  This position is the first point of contact for all visitors to the Wellness Center and provides clerical and administrative support.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Serving as an initial point of contact for students, parents, and visitors, ensuring a warm, welcoming, and inclusive environment Answering incoming phone calls and messages; responding to messages via email and sending triages to the clinical staff Recognizes a student in distress or in need of immediate care and assist in directing them to the appropriate staff member for assistance Scheduling student appointments and guiding students through check in and check out per policies and procedures Provides support for inbound/outbound document processing and maintaining electronic health records according to Student Health Services' confidentiality policy, HIPAA and best practices Assist and maintain immunization records for New York State compliance, both paper form and EMR. Understand and use basic medical terminology Ensure that all student personal and insurance information is updated at the time of each visit Supporting efficient and accurate maintenance of office supplies, facilities, and equipment Upholding confidentiality of all health and wellness support services in the Student Health Services, and other locations Actively participate in integrated Health and Wellness meetings, committees, and student-focused activities Provide assistance and logistical support for department, Health and Wellness programming Attending department, division and university meetings and participate on other committees as requested Performing other job-related duties and responsibilities as assigned Provides coverage for the Counseling Center as needed Maintains the schedule for the Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant, Nurse, and Nurse Manager. Maintains all currently active and archived medical records including scanning all incoming medical records into EMR document files. Completes all required data entry into Point and Click Responsible for maintaining documentation for all department credit card transactions Responsible for supervising and training all student workers within the health center. Train new employees on Electronic Medical Records and Office Policy and Procedures. Maintain patient statistics and compile reports as requested. Coordinates and maintains the scheduling of all Health and Wellness team huddles and department meetings, ensuring alignment with staff availability, departmental priorities, and the needs of a student-centered care model. Develop proficiency in Workday and provide ongoing administrative support related to health center operations, such as processing requisitions, tracking expenses, entering receipts, managing staff schedules, and supporting student employment tasks. Assists in developing agendas and facilitating follow-up for team huddles and meetings in collaboration with clinical and administrative leadership. Tracks attendance and documents key discussion points, outcomes, and action items to support team effectiveness and student support continuity. Supports ongoing internal assessment efforts by collecting and organizing feedback related to service delivery, communication, and student engagement. Assists in the review and improvement of departmental workflows and communication processes, with a focus on delivering holistic, student-centered care that reflects best practices in college health. Engages in student-centered outreach efforts by occasionally tabling in high-traffic areas (e.g., near the dining hall), supporting small-scale wellness programs, and attending selected evening events to enhance visibility and promote health and wellness services to students. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Associates degree or equivalent relevant experience required. Minimum of 3 years of experience in a medical office, hospital or other medical setting; college office experience will be considered. Demonstrated ability to work in a team oriented, fast-paced work environment with a demonstrated ability to meet deadlines, anticipating the needs of the team, and delivering outcomes  Proficient with current medical office technologies Comfortable with medical terminology and discussing personal/sensitive health matters Ability to work with confidential information and maintain strict confidentiality Good communication and teamwork skills Exceptional customer service skills Willing to learn new skills and technologies Ability to maintain a high level of enthusiasm and energy, while portraying a positive image Ability to balance requests from several people and have proven ability to prioritize tasks with conflicting deadlines, handle frequent interruptions, work in an open office environment Demonstrated excellent problem solving; analytical and critical thinking skills Ability to work independently with minimal supervision Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $20.00 - $24.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Pep-Band-Director-Instructor_JR100343": {
      "title": "Pep Band Director/Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Director of the Pep Band is a part-time position that is vital to creating the spirited, energetic atmosphere that defines Le Moyne's athletic events - especially at home men's and women's basketball games and other major college functions. Post-season travel is to be expected in the event that any college team is selected for conference and NCAA tournaments. The Director will play a key role in fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment for student musicians, ensuring that all members feel valued and supported in their musical and personal growth. This is a part time 12-month position working 20 hours per week. This position has primary reporting to the Music Program Director and secondary reporting to the Athletics Director/AVP, Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Performances & Appearances: Attend, direct, and facilitate Pep Band performances and appearances. Collaborate with Athletics and Spirit Squad staff on performance logistics. Coordinate transportation, setup, and other logistical needs for performances. Promote the Pep Band through campus engagement and marketing initiatives. Foster a sense of community and school spirit among student musicians. Practice & Rehearsals: Schedule and conduct rehearsals (minimum of one per week) to prepare the Pep Band for performances. Administrative Responsibilities & Scheduling: Oversee Pep Band member participation, scheduling, and engagement, in close collaboration with Athletics and other College offices. Communicate and coordinate with the music program as appropriate. Maintenance & Inventory: Manage and maintain instruments, equipment, and uniforms. Performance & Safety: Support the safety and well-being of all Pep Band members during practices, travel, and performances. Collaborate with Le Moyne staff to prepare emergency response plans aligned with college protocols. Follow guidance provided by Le Moyne Sports Medicine and relevant departments. Music Instructor Requirement to instruct one section of MUS 395 (1-credit course) per Fall and Spring semester. All Pep Band members who are Le Moyne College students will be required to register for this course each semester of their involvement. Additional Responsibilities Maintain active and positive relationships with area high school band directors and others within the recruiting region Initial recruitment goals are 10-15 new students each fall with an annual ensemble enrollment of 30 plus students. Cultivate positive alumni and community relationships Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Master's degree in Music, Education, or a related field required. Experience leading a band or similar ensemble, preferably at the collegiate or high school level. Strong musical leadership skills. Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and during game-day events. Familiarity with drumline instruction and coordination, particularly in a marching or athletic band setting; ability to integrate percussion effectively into high-energy performances is strongly preferred. Additional Information: Pay Range: $15,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Occupational-Therapist-and-Community-Program-Leader_JR100347": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                         The Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader is responsible for planning, implementing, and evaluating community-based occupational therapy services that promote healthy aging, independence, and fall prevention for older adults. This position provides evidence-informed fall prevention programming, functional assessments, home safety education, and wellness interventions while collaborating with community organizations throughout Central New York. Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader assists with program development, participant outcome measurement, data management, and community outreach to support CARE's mission of improving the health, safety, and quality of life of older adults. This is a part time position working 25 hours per week. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receival of those funds. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Occupational Therapy and Fall Prevention Conduct standardized assessments to identify fall risk, balance deficits, mobility limitations, and functional performance among older adults. Implement CARE's evidence-informed fall prevention and healthy aging programs in community settings. Develop individualized recommendations and intervention strategies to improve balance, strength, mobility, confidence, and safe participation in daily activities. Provide education on fall prevention, home safety, aging in place, adaptive strategies, and healthy aging to participants, caregivers, and community organizations. Conduct home safety evaluations and provide recommendations for environmental modifications and adaptive equipment when appropriate. Monitor participant progress and modify interventions as needed to maximize outcomes. Collaborate with healthcare professionals, senior service agencies, community organizations, and residential facilities to coordinate services and promote participant success. Assist with supervision and mentoring of occupational therapy students during fieldwork experiences, as assigned. Community Programming and Program Development Deliver group education sessions and evidence-informed exercise components that support CARE's healthy aging and fall prevention initiatives. Assist in the development, implementation, and evaluation of new occupational therapy and healthy aging programs. Collaborate with CARE staff to expand programming and strengthen partnerships throughout the community. Develop educational materials, participant resources, and program content that support healthy aging and fall prevention initiatives. Participate in community outreach events, health fairs, workshops, and presentations representing CARE and Le Moyne College. Data Management and Program Evaluation Collect, maintain, and analyze participant outcome data from CARE's fall prevention programs, ensuring accurate and timely entry into the CAMS reporting system. Prepare and submit monthly reports summarizing program outcomes, participation metrics, and performance data for the Onondaga County Office for Aging and other stakeholders. Monitor data quality and reporting compliance within the CAMS reporting system, utilizing findings to support program evaluation, continuous quality improvement, and grant reporting. Analyze program outcome data to identify trends, measure program effectiveness, and support strategic planning and funding initiatives. Develop and deliver annual presentations highlighting program outcomes, community impact, and key performance metrics to county partners, funding organizations, and prospective stakeholders. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Graduate degree in Occupational Therapy from an accredited program. Current New York State Occupational Therapy license in good standing. Experience working with older adults, community-based practice, fall prevention, health promotion, or wellness programming preferred. Experience conducting standardized assessments and interpreting participant outcomes preferred. Excellent organizational, project management, and computer skills. Excellent group facilitation, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. Comfort with basic digital tools for content sharing and creation (e.g., Canva, Instagram, Facebook, Zoom, Microsoft Office, etc.). Ability to collect, analyze, and report program outcome data using electronic reporting systems, including the CAMS reporting system. Experience preparing reports and presenting program outcomes to community partners, stakeholders, and funding organizations preferred. Ability to establish and maintain collaborative relationships with participants, caregivers, community partners, healthcare professionals, and students. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of an interdisciplinary team. Enthusiasm for CARE's mission of promoting healthy aging, fall prevention, and community-based wellness. Must possess a reliable vehicle for travel throughout Central New York. Additional Information: Pay Range: $38.00 - $40.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Crime-Analyst_JR100336-1": {
      "title": "Crime Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Crime Analyst will work on-site at the Syracuse Police Department Crime Analysis Center. The Center is staffed with a team of crime analysts and sworn law enforcement members who support area law enforcement agencies in their efforts to track and reduce Part I Crime. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Perform a variety of research and analytical tasks. Collect, compile, validate, interpret, and analyze data and trends using standard practices and techniques of crime and/or law enforcement intelligence analysis. Perform statistical, spatial, and/or qualitative analyses as needed, making use of standard software packages. Work on assignments that are moderately complex under direct or indirect supervision, where there is latitude for independent action and decision-making. Prepare and deliver reports and presentations of analytic results and may be subpoenaed to testify in court proceedings. Provide crime analysis and criminal intelligence support to law enforcement as they respond to, investigate, and otherwise address criminal activity. Any other relevant duties as assigned by supervisor. Flexibility to work evening/weekend shifts will be required. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in criminal justice, criminology, public administration, or a related field 0-1 year experience in the field of criminology, criminal justice research, or criminal justice policy. Strong written and verbal communication skills are essential. Communication with all police ranks as well as local, state, and federal agencies may be necessary. Knowledge of the criminal justice process. Understanding of basic social science research methods: concepts and techniques of measurement and analysis, and interpretation of results. Experience with databases, spreadsheets, statistical computing, and/or geographic information systems is desired. Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range :  $66,000 - $71,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace.  We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Analyst--Data_JR100341": {
      "title": "Senior Analyst, Data",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Senior Data Analyst for the Institutional Research department will assist leadership in implementing self-service, routine reporting through the development of standardized data management, retrieval and reporting tools, and working with the Director will assist the senior administration with strategic reporting and analytics. In addition to supporting the Director in the development of strategy and tactics for the IR office, the incumbent will coordinate and complete mandatory, periodic, and ad-hoc institutional reporting to maintain compliance with accrediting bodies, government agencies, college guidebooks, and other internal and external requesters. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Extract/collect, clean, analyze, and summarize data for internal use, external surveys (e.g. U.S. News and World Report, college guidebooks, rankings), government and agency mandated reporting (e.g. CDS, IPEDS, NYSED, NCAA), and continued accreditation (e.g. Middle States). Administrate and analyze each survey: Senior survey, Alumni survey; campus climate survey. Work with the HEDS organization on use of other student surveys, etc. Collaborate with the Director on market research for new and existing academic programs. Coordinate college offices, Information Technology, and outside vendors to envision and transform the College's processes for data management, analysis, and reporting. Collaborate across college offices including Financial Aid, Registrar, Finance and Administration, Enrollment Management, and Human Resources to collect and fulfill mandatory, periodic, and ad-hoc institutional reporting. Create and clearly summarize information to support institutional policies and planning, institution-wide assessment, program evaluation, and retention studies. Maintain the accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality of all College data and information. Embody Le Moyne's mission-based competencies of communication, leadership, collaboration, integrity, diversity, and service.   Assist with course evaluations and analysis with the Provost office. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in statistics, economics, computer science, and/or business analytics/data analytics required, Master’s degree in an analytical discipline such as the social sciences, education research, public policy, or related field preferred. 5+ years' experience progressively responsible experience in institutional research, applied analytics, data science, program evaluation, or a related quantitative field; equivalent combinations of graduate education and professional experience will be considered. A minimum of two years' experience in higher education or similar institutional setting. A strong aptitude in using data bases, query tools, etc. A strong understanding of research methodology in behavioral sciences or education measurement. In-depth knowledge of research methods in the social sciences and familiarity with intermediate to advanced multivariate statistical analysis techniques. Demonstrated ability collect/extract, clean, analyze, and summarize data, including competency with analytical software such as SAS and SPSS, Informer, and data visualization software, such as Tableau. Experience with education ERPs such as Workday and Datatel/Colleague preferred. Experience creating and clearly summarizing information for decision makers and other end users. Understanding and applied knowledge of digital transformation processes related to business process and cultural/organizational change. Demonstrated ability to work with less technically-savvy users to develop the scope of reporting, data requirements, and appropriate tools for extraction and reporting. Strong management, interpersonal skills, including active listening, flexibility, and empathy to accurately obtain information from and provide information to client offices and senior leadership. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 64,000 - $72,000 Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Student-Advocate--LPP_JR100338": {
      "title": "Student Advocate, LPP",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY The Student Advocate fosters a program environment conducive to the academic, social, and personal development of students in grades 8-12. Our goal is to help students stay in school, graduate, and plan for their future. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Partner individually with students through targeted mentorship to build self-direction and actionable paths toward future goals. Motivating students collectively and individually to achieve academic success through encouraging, advising, and planning strategies. Providing academic assistance to students including tutoring, homework assistance, and exam review in all subject areas, and assistance in standardized test preparation. Encouraging student completion and reviewing of PLP’s and SEA’s to drive individual case management. Handling other duties as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree NYS K-12 Teaching Certification preferred An interest in, and commitment to, academic achievement for high school students An understanding of and comfort with culturally diverse populations Excellent written and oral communication skills Flexibility and adaptability are essential Additional Information: Pay Range:  $18.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Student-Advocate--LPP_JR100339": {
