    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Campus-Ministry--Retreat-Ministry-and-Faith-Formation_JR100330": {
      "title": "Campus Ministry, Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Campus Ministry The Office of Campus Ministry provides opportunities for students, staff, and faculty to grow spiritually, to engage in local, domestic, and international service and social justice opportunities, to make spiritual retreats, reflect on contemporary social issues and to actively practice their faith. Campus Ministry welcomes and serves persons of all religious affiliations and faith traditions. Position Summary                                                                            Under the supervision of the Director of The Grace Center for Faith and Community and in collaboration with the Campus Ministry Staff, the Campus Minister for Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation promotes the deepening of an active faith and spiritual life, personal and communal, among the students of Le Moyne College. The primary ministry is to create vibrant programing, robust retreat offerings, individual and communal prayer/discernment opportunities, and community centered activities that help deepen, renew, or begin a personal relationship with God. This work is accomplished through a strong understanding of Ignatian spirituality and the stages of faith formation in young adults. This position requires a person who will creatively and strategically develop new programs/mediums and refine existing programs based on the ongoing assessment of student needs and interests. This is an 11 month position that works from August through June.   Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Create a compelling vision for and develop a dynamic portfolio of retreats and other experiences which will engage students in various aspects of faith formation and spiritual development.  Implement all aspects of the retreat program and other faith formation opportunities for students based on class year (First Year Student Retreat, Senior Retreat etc.) as well as topic based (Kairos, Busy Student Retreat, Health & Wellness Retreat, Silent Retreat).  Create new retreat and faith formation opportunities for students of all faiths and for those with no religious beliefs.  Promote opportunities to learn about and practice Ignatian Spirituality.  Create and maintain assessment measures for the program.  Recruit, mentor, develop and empower student leaders who support the retreat program.      Reserve and coordinate the use of various retreat facilities and college vans. Coordinate the OCIA & Confirmation program. Work with faith and service-based student organizations. Keep and maintain accurate budget records for all programs. Maintain a respectful environment for a diverse population of students; embrace diversity in the College and greater community, and treat students as individuals. Work collaboratively with the Grace Center team and campus partners Serve, as needed, as a mentor for Campus Ministry's Service opportunities Assist with local service/outreach initiatives. Serve as a Campus Ministry presence at Sunday Mass and attend all special liturgies of the college. Attend and be visible at various religious services on campus, including but not limited to weekly Jumu'ah prayer and Protestant worship. Attending and being visible at various campus events, including but not limited to sporting, musical, lectures, and other social events. Contribute to Mission Integration divisional meetings, webinars and committees Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree preferred, Bachelor's Degree required in Pastoral Studies, theology or a related field. An understanding of the principles of Ignatian spirituality, the Spiritual Exercises of St. Ignatius, the mission of Jesuit education, and Catholic Social Teaching. Desire to work with a diverse faith community of undergraduate college students. Familiarity with Karios retreat program. Knowledge of O.C.I.A. High level of initiative and imagination. Flexibility to work extended and/or off-hours to meet program needs. Ability to relate and collaborate with various groups both within the Le Moyne College community and the larger Syracuse community. Ability to maintain confidentiality, be self-directed and motivated, possess a high energy level and positive attitude. Knowledge of computers, emphasis on Microsoft Office, Excel, Gmail and various social media platforms. Strong organization and administrative skills. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 57,158 - $59,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/HVAC-Mechanic_JR100316": {
      "title": "HVAC Mechanic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary The HVAC Mechanic is responsible for the repair, maintenance, operation, adjustment and installation of heating, air conditioning, refrigeration equipment, and related control systems. Principal Duties and Essential Functions: Install, repair, adjust, service and maintain electric or pneumatic control systems for heating, ventilation, air conditioning, humidity, laboratory equipment, including calibration of related instruments, gauges and controls. Install, operate, service, and repair conventional mechanical refrigeration/air conditioning equipment including standard refrigerators, and general air conditioning units. Repair, clean, adjust, and/or install oil and gas burners and auxiliary heating specialties other than high-pressure equipment. Conduct necessary tests of equipment to determine malfunctions or causes of breakdown; remove and replace faulty parts, subassemblies and major components; re-test equipment with repaired components and make required adjustments and corrections. Recommend ordering of necessary parts and supplies for maintenance of equipment. Maintain air compressors, air dryers, and low voltage installations such as warning light systems. Instruct and advise users of proper operation of equipment. May be required to make emergency repairs at hours other than normal schedule. May direct helpers and other tradesmen in performance of duties. Calibrate gas ovens and electric grills. Install additional electrical/plumbing components to improve performance or for adaptation of existing systems. Perform duties outside classification incidental to the responsibilities of the Physical Plant Department or such duties assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Five years minimum experience in HVAC trade with working knowledge of steam hydronic and forced air heating, refrigeration, gas electric, pneumatic and direct digital control systems. Knowledge of heating, refrigeration/air conditioning equipment and/or pneumatic and electrical control systems as applicable to work specialty. Experience with steam, hot water and chilled water systems. Provides their own tools, and knows materials, methods and hazards of trade. Skill in the use of tools of the trade. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job, including heavy lifting. Must possess a valid NYS Driver’s license. EPA certification for Refrigerant Handling. May have to work overtime hours on an intermittent basis when operational needs arise . Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range:  $28.33 - $30.32 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Admission-Couselor_JR100327": {
      "title": "Senior Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Admission Counselor is responsible to educate incoming freshman, transfers, parents and counselors about Le Moyne College and the overall college admission process and manage all aspects of college admission including recruitment, counseling, academic advising and evaluation of prospective students and applicants. This position is based at Le Moyne College in Syracuse, NY with a main recruitment territory of Metro NY. This position requires travel to the Metro NY area for student recruitment.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Contribute to the design, development and execution of marketing and recruitment strategies to drive enrollment growth by collaborating with the Director and admission team.  Successfully manage assigned primary, secondary and tertiary geographic territories, conducting extensive travel to build pipelines, lead recruitment events and expand institutional reach.   Counsel, advise and interview prospective first-year and transfer students to guide them through the enrollment lifecycle. Evaluate prospective students’ application materials for final recommendations on admission decisions. Engage in targeted telemarketing and outreach activities to prospective students and applicants. Assist in the coordination and execution of campus open house recruitment events. Plan and host on campus programs for specific student demographics. Maximizes opportunities regarding the college admission process and access to Le Moyne College by delivering inclusive, culturally sensitive guidance to diverse students, parents and counselors. Plans travel and recruitment in the Metro NY area: Visit high schools, junior colleges and multicultural agencies to educate students and counselors about Le Moyne College to build relationships and expand College visibility Conduct off campus interviews during recruiting trips. Engage with local alumni during travel to strengthen relationships and support local enrollment initiatives Represent Le Moyne College at organized off campus recruiting programs including, college nights, national and regional colleges, fairs and mini days. Plan, schedule, and present at Student Information Sessions in targeted geographic areas. (off-campus receptions) Plan, schedule, and present at off campus guidance counselor breakfasts, dinners and association meetings. Participate in panel presentations at secondary schools when invitations are extended to us. Coordinate or assist with other admission related events and programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited College or University required. Experience working in an admission office preferred. Valid Driver’s License required. Excellent oral, presentation and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and time management. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Flexibility and willingness to work extended hours during various time periods including evenings and weekends. High level of initiative and imagination. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish is preferred, but not required. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $24.00 - $27.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Registrar_JR100317": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Assistant Registrar is responsible for all functions within the Registrar’s Office as it relates to student records, degree completion, and curriculum management. In collaboration with other Assistant/Associate Registrars, this position will support the oversight of operations within the Registrar’s Office to ensure successful and efficient performance.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Contribute to the day-to-day operations of the Registrar’s office. Interpret and enforce Federal, State, and College policies, rules, and regulations as appropriate. Maintain data integrity of student academic records. Provide excellent customer service to the constituents of the Registrar’s Office (i.e. students, families, faculty, staff, external agencies, etc.) regarding student records. Commencement and degree completion, including but not limited to: Academic advising to support degree completion Related communications with students, faculty, and staff to support degree persistence and student success. Graduation applications, degree audits, degree conferrals, and data reporting. Collaboration with campus-wide partners to ensure the accuracy and integrity of student records data associated with commencement, honors, awards, and degree conferral activities. Processing of student hiatuses and related communications. Study abroad and international transfer credit analysis in collaboration with various administrators and offices across campus. National Clearinghouse and NSLDS enrollment reporting, degree verification, and error resolutions. Maintenance of document management and workflow solutions, including OnBase, Google forms, and related technologies. Serve as the primary liaison for student systems vendors and external partners, including National Student Clearinghouse and Parchment as well as additional technologies as needed. Assist the Registrar’s Office with: All communications to and from the Registrar’s office, including phone calls, emails, and official correspondences. Maintenance of student educational records. The identification, investigation and resolution of issues and processing errors regarding registration and records areas. Streamlining policies and procedures to improve efficiency. Evaluate, implement, and test new software, upgrades, and new systems utilized in the Registrar’s Office. Development of training materials and serve as the College’s training resource for best practices within student information systems, supportive software, reporting, and solutions for student information systems (SIS) and related software. Serve on selected college committees. Attendance at College events as needed (some evenings and weekends). Other duties as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications     Bachelor’s degree and 2-5 years of related experience in a higher education setting (experience in a Registrar’s Office is preferred). Professional demeanor and ability to interact well with others in a fast-paced operation. Strong knowledge of student records administration, academic operations, and higher education business processes. Demonstrated ability to analyze complex issues, develop practical solutions, and lead operational improvements. Strong interpersonal, leadership, communication, and organizational skills as well as proven ability to work collaboratively. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines effectively. Attention to detail and proficiency in Excel is essential. Respect for confidential information; working knowledge of FERPA is required. Experience with Colleague Datatel, Unity OnBase, Parchment, and Informer is preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $63,300 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Admission_JR100326": {
