    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Professional-Tutor--STEP_JR100314": {
      "title": "Professional Tutor, STEP",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. STEP Program The Le Moyne College Science and Technology Entry Program (STEP) is one of 51 STEP programs in New York State preparing economically disadvantaged students from Nottingham High School, Henninger High School, Syracuse Middle Schools and all of Onondaga County for college. Collaborating with the New York State Department of Education and the Syracuse City School District since 1987, we’re proud of our students’ pursuit of careers in math, science, technology and the health-related or licensed professions. Position Summary  The professional tutor is a vital link between our STEP students (grades 8th – 12th in the Syracuse City School District) and other professional staff within the program. The professional tutor functions as a student advocate and role model and assists program participants to achieve both academic and professional success. This is a part-time position for 2-3 Saturdays per month from 9am-1:30pm. There are a total of 21 Saturdays over the academic school year. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receival of those funds.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position:  Perform one-on-one meetings with students in the program to assist with short and long-range educational goals. Provide academic and professional counseling including assistance with college application process and employment applications; and identify students who require additional academic support services. Facilitate seminars and programming with the assistance of other STEP professionals that contribute to the goal of advancing student's academic, personal, and professional growth. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree required, Science majors preferred (biology, chemistry, or related) NYS Teaching certificate preferred.  An interest in, and commitment to, high school students. Commitment to, and comfort with, culturally diverse populations. Excellent communication skills required. This is a position includes 2-3 Saturdays per month (21 over the academic year) Flexibility and adaptability are essential. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $20.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Associate-Athletic-Director--External-Affairs_JR100310": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Athletic Director, External Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Sr. Associate Athletic Director for External Affairs is a key member of the Athletic leadership team, responsible for the strategic vision, oversight, and execution of all external units within Le Moyne College Athletics. This role is directly accountable for driving departmental revenue, elevating the game-day fan experience, and modernizing sports information and digital media strategies. By unifying corporate partnerships, ticket operations, marketing, and media relations, the Sr. Associate AD ensures a seamless, high-energy fan experience that builds institutional visibility, engages the campus and local communities, and converts fan affinity into long-term financial stability. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Revenue Generation & Strategic Planning (30%) Provide oversight for the identification, solicitation, and closure of new corporate sponsorship agreements Oversee the management of existing partner relationships, ensuring complete contract fulfillment, in-game asset delivery, and multi-year renewals. Provide strategic oversight for the ticket office. Develop and execute aggressive strategies for season, group, mini-plan, and single-game ticket packages to maximize venue capacity and optimize revenue. Explore and establish targets for alternative revenue opportunities, including premium seating, hospitality experiences, merchandise licensing, and digital content monetization. Utilize data analytics and market research to provide regular revenue forecasting, attendance metrics, and strategic performance analysis to the Athletic Director/AVP. Fan Experience & Game Atmosphere Production (30%) Own the overall atmosphere of all home sporting events to ensure a vibrant home-court advantage. Direct and approve all in-game creative elements, music, public address scripts, video board content, and promotional activations. Lead and coordinate game-day stakeholders—including the pep band, cheer/dance squads, spirit groups, and third-party game staff—to maintain a professional, high-energy environment. Collaborate with campus partners to design and execute innovative theme nights, giveaways, and community relations initiatives to increase attendance among students, faculty, staff, and the broader Central New York public. Sports Information, Communications & Brand Development (30%) Oversee and actively contribute to the sports information and communications unit. Direct strategies to build positive relationships with local, regional, and national media to generate national storytelling opportunities. Supervise the coordination of content for the official athletics website and all social media platforms. Establish strict proofing and layer-of-approval processes for public-facing digital materials to ensure strict alignment with college brand standards. Ensure the accurate production of all sports media guides, historical archiving, and live game-day statistics operations. Leadership, Sport Administration & Compliance (10%) Serve on the Athletic Director/AVP’s senior staff, actively contributing to department-wide strategic planning and decision-making. Serve as the designated Sport Administrator for selected athletic programs, providing operational guidance and evaluating head coaches. Maintain strict adherence to and up-to-date knowledge of all NCAA Division I, conference, and institutional rules, regulations, and deadlines. Ensure the physical, emotional, and social welfare of all student-athletes. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Business, Communications, or a related field required; Master’s degree preferred. 7+ years of progressive, full-time experience in sports marketing, revenue generation, or athletic communications, preferably within NCAA Division I athletics. Proven track record of leading, managing, and developing a diverse staff of department area heads, graduate assistants, and interns. Ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally in both written and verbal forms. Proven ability to work constructively and collaboratively within a team environment and across diverse departments. Strong critical thinking skills with the ability to identify issues, propose solutions, and adapt to changing workplace needs. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, respectful, and equitable environment for all colleagues, clients, and stakeholders Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks effectively, and manage multiple projects simultaneously Demonstrated commitment to ethical conduct, honesty, and professional integrity in all workplace interactions Must possess a valid, current U.S. driver’s license. Must have reliable transportation or the ability to rent a vehicle when needed to travel. May need to drive campus vehicles for local events. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Alumni-and-Donor-Relations_JR100311": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Alumni and Donor Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Director for Alumni and Donor Relations plays a vital role in planning and executing signature alumni and donor events, with primary responsibility for the logistics of Reunion Weekend and annual fundraising dinners. In addition, this position assists with athletic alumni programming, manages a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects and supports the daily administrative operations of the Alumni and Donor Relations team. The role requires excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, volunteers, and vendors to deliver high-quality experiences that strengthen connections and inspire philanthropy. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Event Management (Primary Focus) Serve as the lead project manager for Reunion Weekends, overseeing logistics, vendor coordination, volunteer support, and event communications. Plan and execute annual fundraising dinners, coordinating with Advancement, Facilities, Catering, and external vendors to deliver high-caliber donor experiences. Assist in the planning and execution of athletic alumni events, working closely with colleagues in Athletics and Advancement. Support other alumni and donor events as needed, including regional gatherings, networking programs, and recognition events. Alumni and Donor Engagement Build strong relationships with alumni volunteers, reunion committees, and event participants. Carry a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects, engaging them through personalized outreach, event invitations, and stewardship. Assist with donor recognition activities connected to events, including program booklets, signage, and acknowledgments. Team and Administrative Support Provide day-to-day administrative support for the Alumni and Donor Relations team, including budget tracking, event registration management, and database updates. Serve as the point of contact for vendors, alumni inquiries, and internal partners related to event logistics. Contribute to Advancement communications, including event promotions, email campaigns, and website updates Collaboration Partner with colleagues across Advancement and the College to ensure events and engagement initiatives align with institutional priorities. Represent the College at alumni, donor, and campus events, occasionally requiring evening or weekend work. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 3+years of experience in event planning, alumni relations, donor relations, or related fields. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple complex events simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong relationship-building skills with alumni, donors, and volunteers. Proficiency with Microsoft Office; experience with event management platforms and advancement databases (e.g., Raiser’s Edge) preferred. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and travel for events as needed. Commitment to the College’s Jesuit values of service, excellence, and cura personalis (care for the whole person). Ability to occasional work evenings and weekends. Ability to travel to support alumni and donor events as needed. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $25.00 - $27.50 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Coach--Tennis_JR100260": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Tennis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Coach for Men’s and Women’s Tennis is responsible for providing assistance and support for the conduct of a comprehensive, high quality NCAA Division I men’s and women’s tennis program, within the guidelines of all rules and policies established by the department, the institution, the NEC Conference, and the NCAA, in accordance with the academic standards, and the stated mission of Le Moyne College and the Athletic Department, including the advancement of its “Inside the L“ shared culture. This position will require daily and/or weekly duties and tasks as assigned by the head coach which require exercising discretion and independent judgment consisting of 75% instructional and 25% recruitment/administrative activities. This is a ten month position from August 1st through May 31st. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: NCAA Compliance Assist program in compliance with all applicable NCAA, conference, and institutional policies, rules and regulations. Assist with timely submission of all compliance related work flows through Teamworks to maintain the highest levels of integrity and transparency. Maintain open and responsive communications with the Associate Director of Compliance Maintain up to date certification in all required areas (NCAA DI Institute Modules, 1st Aid/CPR/AED Training, Etc). Fiscal Management Assist with all budget requests, documentation, receipts and related forms and paperwork, according to existing policy and established deadlines as assigned by head coach. Enrollment Management Assist leading and supporting the College Enrollment Management priorities through partnership, participation, and meeting goals with Enrollment Management initiatives as assigned by head coach. Assist the department with its gender equity planning and the satisfaction of all Title IX legislation by striving to attain goals related to any applicable enrollment management initiatives within your particular program as assigned by head coach. Assist head coach with responding to all requests for information from prospective student-athletes, coaches, parents, and/or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with solicit information from and distribute information to eligible prospective student-athletes and coaches and or parents or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with developing and distributing appropriate recruiting materials, publications and information to interested prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with maintaining accurate and comprehensive recruiting records of all prospective student athletes. College and Department Service It is expected that employees have a willingness and commitment to be broadly engaged and in service to the College as demonstrated through participation on committees and attendance at College functions/events. It is expected that employees participate with department committees, as elected or assigned, to develop, evaluate and enhance department policy. Attendance at all departmental meetings, unless excused in advance by the AVP for Athletics, is expected while a commitment to the College's priorities and the department's goals and objectives are vital to the success of the position. Academic Support Assist head coach with providing the appropriate academic support, assistance, motivation and environment for student-athletes. Become familiar with appropriate academic resource and assistance programs available to student-athletes. Assist head coach with monitoring the academic progress of your student-athletes from current class work to graduation. Understand current institutional academic standards and policies. Game Management Assist head coach with working with appropriate personnel to determine your needs for the organization, coordination, and scheduling of all home and away contests including:  facility and equipment set-up, officials, scorekeepers, statisticians, media considerations, lodging, meals, travel arrangements, etc. Sports Performance Submit all paperwork, schedule meetings and respond to all information requests from athletic trainers and team physicians according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Head Athletic Trainer as assigned by head coach. All decisions regarding the health and safety of student athletes when it comes to physical participation is at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Assist head coach with coordinating with Head Strength/Conditioning Coach on the conduct of a comprehensive training program to enhance both personal and performance growth/development. Sports Information Respond to all information requests and work with the media, etc. according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications as assigned by head coach. Always inform the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications when you or any of your athletes has been contacted by the media. Fund Raising Assist head coach with fund raising activities. Particular attention should be given to NCAA legislation surrounding booster groups and donors. Reconciliation of all revenues and deposits should be handled in accordance with institutional and departmental policy. Community Service A commitment to community services is an important tenant of the College's mission and to that end it is anticipated that employees will be involved in various community activities as a representative of the Le Moyne College Athletics Department. Assist head coach with identifying and cultivating a community partnership with a service-based organization to provide an impactful service experience for your student-athletes. Professional Development Opportunities to maintain and advance current understandings of techniques, strategies, theories, and regulations as they relate to the athletics industry are essential. Attendance and participation in conferences is strongly encouraged if assigned by head coach. Supervisory Relationships For purpose of performance evaluations and most other official duties, the first level of contact for the Assistant Coach is with the Head Coach. Appeals of decisions are to be taken to the Director of Athletics. Functional Relationships/Secondary Sources: All coaches are expected to work cooperatively with all members of the Athletic Department (Administrators, Support Staff, Colleagues), and any other campus (admissions, housing, financial aid, maintenance, etc), or community office/agency that you might be involved with. Communications and required documentation should be handled in a timely manner. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned.      QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree preferred. 1 to 2 years of progressive experience in the conduct of a collegiate level tennis program with proven success in recruiting high quality student athletes and/or equivalent related experiences. Knowledge of and ability to apply NCAA and NEC conference rules as they pertain to tennis programs. The successful candidate will be required to be First Aid/CPR/AED certified and to complete all required NCAA DI recruiting education modules prior to being able to participate in off campus recruiting activities and countable athletically related activities. Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills needed. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $17,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Vice-President--Enrollment-Management-and-Marketing_JR100294": {
      "title": "Vice President, Enrollment Management and Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLe Moyne College, a Catholic and Jesuit college located on a 160‑acre suburban campus known as “the Heights” in Syracuse, New York, seeks nominations and applications for its next Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing . Rooted in the Jesuit tradition of cura personalis —care for the whole person—Le Moyne brings together students of all backgrounds in an inclusive, mission‑driven community focused on academic excellence and real-world impact. The College is recognized for its close-knit learning environment, highlighted by a 12:1 student‑to‑faculty ratio, small classes, and faculty who prioritize mentorship and student development. Consistently ranked among the top regional universities in the Northeast, Le Moyne combines rigorous academics across the liberal arts, sciences, business, health professions, and education with strong career preparation outcomes. At Le Moyne, there is a palpable sense of momentum and transformation shaping the institution. The College is investing boldly in its future through expanded academic programs, new partnerships, and significant campus enhancements designed to deepen student learning and engagement. Recent developments include the launch of new programs aligned with emerging fields, major state and philanthropic investments supporting health care and STEM education, and hands‑on research opportunities that allow students to work alongside faculty in nationally and globally relevant settings. At the same time, Le Moyne is reimagining its physical campus with new and renovated spaces that foster collaboration, creativity, and community, alongside the transition to Division I athletics in 2023—an important milestone that is strengthening institutional visibility and school spirit. Together, these initiatives reflect a college on the rise, confidently advancing its Jesuit mission while creating new pathways for student success and impact. The College seeks an accomplished and visionary Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing, who will report directly to President Linda LeMura and: Collaborate with senior leadership across the College. Lead institution-wide enrollment and marketing and serve as a key member of the President’s Leadership Team. Provide strategic and operational leadership for a comprehensive, data-informed enrollment management strategy that advances Le Moyne’s Jesuit mission, academic excellence, financial vitality, and commitment to access and diversity. Oversee undergraduate and graduate admission, financial aid, and communications and marketing. Guide integrated recruitment, retention, branding, and pricing strategies that strengthen enrollment outcomes and institutional reputation. Inspire and develop a high-performing, student-centered team. Leverage analytics and market insights to inform decision-making and optimize institutional resources. Serve as a visible advocate for Le Moyne with prospective students, families, school counselors, and external partners. Bring the vision, judgment, and energy to help shape Le Moyne’s continued momentum and future growth in a collaborative, mission-driven environment. Mission and Vision At Le Moyne College, Jesuit and Catholic values shape everything the institution does, from how it teaches to how members of the community care for one another. Its mission is grounded in cura personalis , the Jesuit principle of caring for the whole person. In practice, this means small classes where students are known by name, faculty who serve as mentors, and an emphasis on service, justice, and lifelong learning. Le Moyne supports students’ growth not only academically, but also personally and ethically, preparing them to lead meaningful lives and make a difference in the world. All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV/resume and a letter of interest. Review of applications has begun and will continue until the position is filled. For fullest consideration, all materials should be received by July 10, 2026 . Please direct all inquiries to Kim Migoya ( kmigoya@wittkieffer.com ). All nominations and applications should be submitted to Amy Crutchfield, Christy Pratt, and Kim Migoya through the WittKieffer Candidate Portal by clicking here . Candidates can also find the portal via the WittKieffer website at www.wittkieffer.com . Le Moyne College estimates the salary range for this position at $200, 000 to $220,000. The College also offers a comprehensive, competitive benefits program. Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship. Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time."
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Programmer-Analyst_JR100283": {
      "title": "Programmer Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Programmer/Analyst is central to maintaining and modernizing the College’s core administrative systems. This position is responsible for the performance, stability, and evolution of our Ellucian Colleague environment while helping transition legacy processes into scalable, modern solutions. The Programmer/Analyst acts as a technical bridge between established systems and emerging technologies—building integrations, reducing technical debt, and enabling more efficient, data-driven operations across the institution. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Maintain and enhance the Ellucian Colleague system and UniData environment to ensure reliability, performance, and data integrity Diagnose and resolve system issues; proactively tune and optimize system performance Develop, modify, and support applications using UniBasic and Envision Create and maintain clear, usable documentation for legacy systems and processes Safeguard sensitive institutional data in alignment with security and compliance standards Reduce technical debt by auditing and streamlining legacy custom code Identify opportunities to replace custom solutions with standard (“baseline”) system functionality Simplify and modernize system architecture to improve maintainability and scalability Decommission obsolete processes, reports, and data structures to support future system upgrades or migrations Design and implement integrations between Colleague and modern platforms (e.g., Canvas, Workday) using APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON Develop reports and data solutions using tools like SQL Server Reporting Services and Informer Support data exchange processes that enable accurate, timely reporting and decision-making across departments Partner with departments such as Financial Aid, Registrar, and Bursar to align business processes with system capabilities Translate functional needs into technical solutions within the Colleague environment Guide stakeholders through changes that reduce reliance on custom development and improve long-term sustainability Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience required 5+ years of programming experience, ideally in ERP or enterprise systems required Experience with SQL Server or similar relational databases required, experience with Ellucian Colleague, UniData, or UniBasic preferred Familiarity with APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON required Strong problem-solving skills and ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions Experience with reporting tools such as Informer or SQL Server Reporting Services preferred Familiarity with systems such as Canvas or Workday preferred Experience in higher education or similarly complex institutional environments preferred Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Student-Success_JR100257": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of the Student Success Center plays a pivotal role in managing the daily operations of the Center and provides professional support to all Center staff, including professionals and student employees. This position coordinates the tutoring program, collaborates closely with colleagues in the Quantitative Research Center and Writing Center, and empowers students to achieve their academic, personal, and professional goals through individualized coaching and resource connection. In addition, the Associate Director leads and supports retention initiatives by identifying enrollment and persistence risks, coordinating proactive outreach efforts, and collaborating with campus partners to strengthen student retention across all class years. This position will commence no earlier than June 1, 2026. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Center Operations/Management - 30% Oversee the Center’s daily operations such as student programming, academic support services and triage Coordinate programming efforts to support students and create visibility for the Center  Partner with colleagues to develop and implement student success initiatives Respond to inquiries from students, families, faculty, and other college personnel Promote the Center’s resources and achievements to external audiences Work collaboratively with coaches to carry out the mission, goals and outcomes of the Student Success Center Provide staff development, including hiring, mentoring, and evaluation of student staff Carry out logistical duties to support academic advising such as compiling administrative withdrawal data, sending hiatus letters, and reaching out to faculty advisors to provide support Promote and contribute to existing student success efforts while assessing their effectiveness and implementing new initiatives Case Management/Academic Coaching - 25% Provide comprehensive academic coaching to a caseload of students who have been referred. (Referrals may come from Student of Concern reports, faculty referrals, assignments based on academic standing, student-initiated requests, etc.) Engage in initiative-taking management of caseload, including consistent and direct contact with students, and targeted outreach at key points in the semester. Troubleshoot registration, billing and financial aid issues that may arise for students. Assess learner needs in order to help them make fully informed decisions about their pathways as well as challenging them to make progress toward their goals. Develop relationships with identified students that encourage continuation of long-term academic coaching into future semesters, as needed. Assist students in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; work with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivate students to practice self-regulation and take ownership of their academic success. Engage at-risk students, providing one-on-one intrusive advising meetings to improve engagement and ensure success. Connect students with other campus resources related to tutoring, spiritual support, disability services, counseling and health, housing and food insecurity, career planning, finances, etc. Partner with faculty, academic advisors, and campus colleagues regarding Student of Concern referrals. Assist instructors with follow-up on students who have been referred through the Student of Concern process for excessive absences, unsatisfactory grades, etc. Record applicable interventions via Maxient. Retention Leadership – 20% Monitor early alerts, absences, GPA risk factors, DFW rates, and withdrawal patterns to identify students who may be at risk for attrition. Coordinate campus-wide retention initiatives in partnership with the Director of Student Success and other stakeholders (Dean Restaurant Nights, Registration Fest, Winter and Summer Academic Bridge). Compile the academic standing data (students on warning/probation) and notify undergraduates each semester when they are not in good academic standing Continually refine programing to support students on probation, assign counselors to support them, and provide ongoing training to counselors Lead targeted persistence campaigns focusing on key transition points (e.g., first-year to sophomore retention, post-hiatus return, students on academic warning/probation). Analyze retention and persistence trends to inform programming, resource allocation, and interventions. Collaborate with Academic Deans, Class Deans, Enrollment Management, Financial Aid, Housing, Athletics, and other departments to ensure coordinated outreach and resolution of barriers to persistence. Serve as the Student Success representative on the retention committee Implement best practices for holistic retention support that address academic, social, financial, and wellbeing risk factors. Contribute retention data insights during departmental and campus-wide meetings. Tutoring Oversight - 15% Organize the hiring, supervision, and regular training of student tutors Oversee tutor payroll and monitor the associated budget Coordinate the administration of study groups that are offered in collaboration with various departments and learning communities, including hiring, training, and payroll for peer leaders, and maintaining records on all group sessions/workshops Continually seek faculty input on tutoring effectiveness and operations Serve as a liaison to other Le Moyne College programs (i.e., the Physician Assistant program, nursing partnerships, etc.) regarding academic support issues and scheduling Maintain tutoring data and provide regular reports and assessments Professional Development - 5% Meet regularly with the Director of Student Success to discuss the status of retention data/efforts. Participate as an active member of the Student Success Center staff meetings and retreats and provide informed feedback and initiative. Serve as a member of key campus committees related to student success Attend division- and campus-wide meetings to keep current on college initiatives, student demographics, program offerings, upcoming trends, etc. Continually review best practices related to student success and relay pertinent information to campus partners as needed. Manage confidential student information with tact, discretion, and in compliance with FERPA regulations Progress Monitoring – 5% Develop and maintain accurate, organized, and detailed student records of students who have sought assistance. Create and maintain student plans in close collaboration with the Director of the Student Success Center to ensure accurate counseling, mitigation of student issues, and ongoing feedback; adjust strategies as needed. Monitor student academic progress by compiling, analyzing, and reporting on student progress utilizing available databases and resources (e.g., Phinfo, Datatel, Informer, WCOnline, CampusGroups) Assess student attrition risk and vulnerability and intervene at critical points of the student's educational path. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree and 5+ years of relevant experience is required or equivalent experience and education. Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Education or related field is preferred. Establish and maintain cooperative and productive relationships with both campus and off-campus contacts, including students, faculty, prospects, parents, and community partners Possess excellent interpersonal and written communication skills Maintain a high level of confidentiality due to the sensitivity of the nature of the student and college information this position requires Experience working directly with college students, preferably with transfer, non-traditional, and/or under-represented student populations, concerning academic success Experience with large- and small-scale event planning Experience with Microsoft Office, Datatel Student Management Software, and familiarity with Course Management Software (e.g. Canvas), Informer, and Slate are preferred Willingness to work evenings and weekends to accommodate student needs and programming Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment Excellent customer service skills Strong written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated time management and organization skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $66,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Annual-Giving_JR100254": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Annual Giving",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of Annual Giving plays a key role in the planning, execution, and management of strategies that drive philanthropic support through annual giving programs. This position focuses on donor acquisition, retention, and upgrading, as well as strengthening engagement among alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of the College. The Associate Director partners closely with colleagues in Advancement, particularly with the Engagement Center, and Marketing and Communications to design multi-channel campaigns that inspire giving and align with institutional priorities. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Support the development and implementation of a comprehensive annual giving plan to achieve participation and revenue goals. Oversee key components of the annual giving program, including direct mail, email, texting, digital campaigns, crowdfunding, and Giving Day. Review giving data and trends to inform segmentation, messaging, and campaign strategies. Collaborate with the Advancement team to identify new opportunities for donor engagement and pipeline growth. Manage a portfolio of annual donors and prospects to cultivate, solicit, and steward gifts Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations to ensure execution of stewardship plans that recognize annual giving donors at all levels. Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations team to integrate giving opportunities into campus and regional events. Supervise and mentor staff, students, and/or volunteers engaged in annual giving efforts. Collaborate across Advancement to ensure consistency and coordination in fundraising messages and donor experiences. Track and report on campaign performance, donor retention, participation rates, and other key metrics. Maintain accurate records in the Raiser’s Edge and GiveCampus CRM systems. Use data to identify trends, test new strategies, and inform long-term planning. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 5+ years of experience in fundraising, annual giving, or related field required, experience in higher education preferred. Demonstrated success managing campaigns or projects from conception through completion. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical skills with experience using data to drive decisions. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to work independently but collaboratively as part of a goal-oriented team. Commitment to the Jesuit mission and values of the College. Familiarity with CRM systems and fundraising software (e.g., Raiser’s Edge, GiveCampus) preferred. Understanding of donor segmentation and digital fundraising techniques preferred. Supervisory and/or volunteer management experience preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $63,000 - $73,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Digital-Content-and-Social-Media-Creator_JR100348": {
      "title": "Digital Content and Social Media Creator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Position Summary                                                                         The Digital Content and Social Media Creator serves as a digital storyteller and brand ambassador for the College, responsible for increasing Le Moyne’s visibility, fostering institutional pride, and engaging a diverse community of prospective and current students, alumni, faculty, staff, and friends. Operating in an energetic, hands-on capacity, the successful candidate will primarily serve as the lead content producer for the College's primary social channels, executing digital campaigns in alignment with overarching departmental strategy. This individual will conceive, shoot, edit, and publish high-impact multimedia content while actively monitoring community interactions and utilizing data-driven insights to optimize reach. This position offers an exciting opportunity for an adaptable, highly creative, and collaborative professional to build on our strong regional reputation and further expand the College's reach. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Content Creation & Storytelling Develops and executes creative content that aligns with designated monthly campaign themes, driving prospective student engagement throughout key stages of the enrollment lifecycle. Plan, script, shoot, edit, and publish high-quality, engaging content across all official, central Le Moyne channels (i.e., Instagram, TikTok, LinkedIn, Facebook, X, YouTube) Gather, capture, and synthesize a wide range of digital media (i.e. photography, news links, quotes, event registration, etc.) into cohesive and impactful content tailored for various platforms and audiences. Leverage content for use on the College’s primary website including feature stories, student spotlights, event recaps, and rich media assets—that are fresh, informative, and aligned with marketing goals. Capture daily campus life, academic achievements, student stories, athletics, and special events in real-time. Comfortably collaborate with students, faculty, and staff. Maintain a cohesive visual identity and authentic brand voice that resonates with prospective students, current students, alumni, the local community, and other constituents. Channel & Community Management Manage daily social media publishing schedules and content calendars. Actively monitor channels to cultivate two-way conversation—responding to comments, direct messages, and brand mentions with warmth, enthusiasm, and accuracy. Serve as the eyes and ears of the college online, fostering a positive, safe, and vibrant online community. Coordinates content reviews and approval workflows, ensuring all assets are vetted prior to publishing Cross-Campus Collaboration Partner proactively with departments across campus to amplify major initiatives and campus stories. Help recruit student workers and coordinate student-created content. Serve as a friendly, approachable liaison who builds trust across every department. Analytics & Optimization Translate data insights into actionable strategies to continuously boost engagement and organic reach. Monitor monthly performance recaps and optimize content accordingly. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree is required. 2–4+ years of professional social media management experience Proven ability to manage projects end-to-end—from initial idea to filming, editing, posting, and measuring—without needing a large production team. Enthusiasm, creativity, and optimism. Ability to thrive in a dynamic environment where news happens fast and priorities shift. Highly approachable, friendly, and outgoing. Equally comfortable walking up to students on campus or collaborating with senior administrators. Expert knowledge of native platform tools (TikTok, IG Reels), capcut/short-form video editing apps, Canva, Adobe Creative Cloud, social scheduling/analytics tools (i.e., Sprout Social, Hootsuite, or similar), and basic experience with Content Management Systems (CMS) for web updates (i.e., WordPress, Cascade, or similar). Comfortable appearing on camera, hosting quick Q&As, or leading video interviews when the content calls for it. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $28.00 - $35.00 per hour (This is an hourly position that calculates to $50,960 - $63,700 annually) Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Manresa-Program_JR100349-1": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Manresa Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Coordinator for Manresa Programs will provide the support needed to serve the students participating in the seminar programs, manage logistics of guest speakers visiting campus, maintain budget controls, assist faculty and staff participating in grant-supported programs, and provide administrative support to the program co-directors. The coordinator will work closely with program co-directors to help Manresa reach its goal of focusing and magnifying the preparation of students for purposeful lives of meaningful success promoted by Le Moyne's Jesuit, liberal arts education. The coordinator will serve as the liaison to the Finance department to ensure compliance with existing and future policies and procedures. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Manresa Seminars (50%) Provide administrative support for the Manresa seminars offered each semester. Tasks include, but are not limited to: Provide direct support to mentors (faculty and staff) through meeting coordination and general problem-solving Maintaining and updating seminar and materials Producing the group materials needed for each seminar Coordinating Facilities and Catering for each seminar Coordinate service opportunities with community partners Monitoring and tracking student progress throughout the semester Maintaining and updating the database of student participant data Coordinate program promotion through print and digital media Attend weekly meetings with professional staff Ensure compliance with College & departmental policies regarding computer usage and personal information Compiling assessment data for later analysis Process invoices and facilitate payments with Accounts Payable Monitor expenses and provide budget updates to the co-directors Assist in preparation of yearly budget reports for grant funders (as applicable) Steward stipends to students and mentors through the payment process Other Manresa Programming (40%) Provide administrative support for Manresa programs outside of the seminar series. These programs could change yearly but planned programs include Purposeful Advising (grant program), Regional Conference, Vocational Companions, Manresa Reading Group, visiting speakers and scholars, and Career Treks.  Tasks include, but are not limited to: Producing the group materials needed for each program Scheduling and room reservations for faculty development seminars, workshops, and retreats Coordinating catering for seminars and workshops Steward stipends to faculty and staff through the payment process Assist in compiling assessment materials of Manresa-related programs  Monitor grant expenditures ○   Assist in producing the interim budget reports for continued grant funding Assist in creation of final budget report to funder(s) Coordinating on-site logistics for visiting speakers and other events Securing transportation and lodging as needed Steward stipends/honoraria through the payment process Tasks specific to Career Treks include: Assisting to prepare students for off-site experiences Creating and monitoring application materials for career treks Secure appropriate transportation and lodging When needed, travel with a co-director to assist in program implementation Collaborate with Alumni Relations staff to plan an alumni event in each city Coordinate with alumni volunteers to finalize hosting details Ensuring assessment measures are implemented and compiled Other responsibilities as assigned (10%) The coordinator is expected to assist staff in Career Advising and Development as needed Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Associate's Degree in Business Management or related field required with 1-2 years of relevant experience, Bachelor's Degree preferred  Managing budgets including accounts payable and general maintenance Demonstrated experience working with confidential information (eg. HIPPA or FERPA) Proven ability to coordinate multiple projects and personnel General knowledge of Higher Education administration and structure Thorough knowledge of G-Suite (Docs, Sheets, etc.) and Microsoft Office Demonstrate strong written & oral communication skills Exceptional interpersonal, organizational, and analytical skills Self-motivated, able to conduct oneself in a highly professional and ethical manner Must be willing to work evening hours from 5:30 pm to 9:30 pm and select weekends as needed Additional Information: Pay Range: $20.00 - $24.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Plumber_JR100352": {
      "title": "Plumber",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Plumbing Mechanic is responsible for the repair, maintenance, operation, adjustment and installation of plumbing fixtures, piping, and equipment. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Install, repair, adjust, service and maintain plumbing drains, water and gas, lines, fixtures and equipment. Inspect plumbing systems, components and perform routine maintenance and repairs. Replace defective pipe, by cutting, bending, soldering and threading defective pipe. Open clogged drains with plumber’s snake or other appropriate tools or devices Replace washers and other worn or defective parts of valves, faucets, shower controls and other similar devices. Be familiar with plumbing codes and regulations including as they relate to food service equipment. Be able to work in biological or anatomical laboratories where human/animal bodies or parts may be expected to worker’s view. Repair or replace damaged plumbing fixtures such as sinks, toilets, showers, and bathtubs and/or connect them to supply and waste pipes using gaskets, couplings, flanges, traps and valves and by soldering connections to make joints as required. As required, estimate materials needed and record time and material expended on each work order. Recommend ordering of necessary parts and supplies for maintenance of equipment. Instruct and advise users of proper operation of equipment. Will be required to make emergency repairs at hours other than normal schedule. May direct helpers and other tradesmen in performance of duties. Install additional plumbing components to improve performance or for adaptation of existing systems. Ordering and installation of necessary lighting, outlets, switches (parts and supplies) for dorm maintenance. Perform duties outside classification incidental to the responsibilities of the Physical Plant Department or such duties assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   High School diploma or equivalent required. Minimum of five years full-time experience in the Plumbing trade with apprenticeship training or equivalent on the job training required. Experience with steam, hot water and chilled water systems required. Provides their own hand tools, and knows materials, methods and hazards of trade. Skill in the use of tools of the trade required. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job, including heavy lifting, working from ladders, scaffolding and lifts required. Must possess a valid NYS Driver’s license. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range:  $26.59 - $28.59 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Coordinator--Student-Health-Services_JR100342": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Health Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   This position provides daily clerical and administrative support to the personnel in the Wellness Center for Health and Counseling.  This position is the first point of contact for all visitors to the Wellness Center and provides clerical and administrative support.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Serving as an initial point of contact for students, parents, and visitors, ensuring a warm, welcoming, and inclusive environment Answering incoming phone calls and messages; responding to messages via email and sending triages to the clinical staff Recognizes a student in distress or in need of immediate care and assist in directing them to the appropriate staff member for assistance Scheduling student appointments and guiding students through check in and check out per policies and procedures Provides support for inbound/outbound document processing and maintaining electronic health records according to Student Health Services' confidentiality policy, HIPAA and best practices Assist and maintain immunization records for New York State compliance, both paper form and EMR. Understand and use basic medical terminology Ensure that all student personal and insurance information is updated at the time of each visit Supporting efficient and accurate maintenance of office supplies, facilities, and equipment Upholding confidentiality of all health and wellness support services in the Student Health Services, and other locations Actively participate in integrated Health and Wellness meetings, committees, and student-focused activities Provide assistance and logistical support for department, Health and Wellness programming Attending department, division and university meetings and participate on other committees as requested Performing other job-related duties and responsibilities as assigned Provides coverage for the Counseling Center as needed Maintains the schedule for the Nurse Practitioner/Physician Assistant, Nurse, and Nurse Manager. Maintains all currently active and archived medical records including scanning all incoming medical records into EMR document files. Completes all required data entry into Point and Click Responsible for maintaining documentation for all department credit card transactions Responsible for supervising and training all student workers within the health center. Train new employees on Electronic Medical Records and Office Policy and Procedures. Maintain patient statistics and compile reports as requested. Coordinates and maintains the scheduling of all Health and Wellness team huddles and department meetings, ensuring alignment with staff availability, departmental priorities, and the needs of a student-centered care model. Develop proficiency in Workday and provide ongoing administrative support related to health center operations, such as processing requisitions, tracking expenses, entering receipts, managing staff schedules, and supporting student employment tasks. Assists in developing agendas and facilitating follow-up for team huddles and meetings in collaboration with clinical and administrative leadership. Tracks attendance and documents key discussion points, outcomes, and action items to support team effectiveness and student support continuity. Supports ongoing internal assessment efforts by collecting and organizing feedback related to service delivery, communication, and student engagement. Assists in the review and improvement of departmental workflows and communication processes, with a focus on delivering holistic, student-centered care that reflects best practices in college health. Engages in student-centered outreach efforts by occasionally tabling in high-traffic areas (e.g., near the dining hall), supporting small-scale wellness programs, and attending selected evening events to enhance visibility and promote health and wellness services to students. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Associates degree or equivalent relevant experience required. Minimum of 3 years of experience in a medical office, hospital or other medical setting; college office experience will be considered. Demonstrated ability to work in a team oriented, fast-paced work environment with a demonstrated ability to meet deadlines, anticipating the needs of the team, and delivering outcomes  Proficient with current medical office technologies Comfortable with medical terminology and discussing personal/sensitive health matters Ability to work with confidential information and maintain strict confidentiality Good communication and teamwork skills Exceptional customer service skills Willing to learn new skills and technologies Ability to maintain a high level of enthusiasm and energy, while portraying a positive image Ability to balance requests from several people and have proven ability to prioritize tasks with conflicting deadlines, handle frequent interruptions, work in an open office environment Demonstrated excellent problem solving; analytical and critical thinking skills Ability to work independently with minimal supervision Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $20.00 - $24.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Pep-Band-Director-Instructor_JR100343": {
      "title": "Pep Band Director/Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Director of the Pep Band is a part-time position that is vital to creating the spirited, energetic atmosphere that defines Le Moyne's athletic events - especially at home men's and women's basketball games and other major college functions. Post-season travel is to be expected in the event that any college team is selected for conference and NCAA tournaments. The Director will play a key role in fostering a welcoming and inclusive environment for student musicians, ensuring that all members feel valued and supported in their musical and personal growth. This is a part time 12-month position working 20 hours per week. This position has primary reporting to the Music Program Director and secondary reporting to the Athletics Director/AVP, Intercollegiate Athletics and Recreation. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Performances & Appearances: Attend, direct, and facilitate Pep Band performances and appearances. Collaborate with Athletics and Spirit Squad staff on performance logistics. Coordinate transportation, setup, and other logistical needs for performances. Promote the Pep Band through campus engagement and marketing initiatives. Foster a sense of community and school spirit among student musicians. Practice & Rehearsals: Schedule and conduct rehearsals (minimum of one per week) to prepare the Pep Band for performances. Administrative Responsibilities & Scheduling: Oversee Pep Band member participation, scheduling, and engagement, in close collaboration with Athletics and other College offices. Communicate and coordinate with the music program as appropriate. Maintenance & Inventory: Manage and maintain instruments, equipment, and uniforms. Performance & Safety: Support the safety and well-being of all Pep Band members during practices, travel, and performances. Collaborate with Le Moyne staff to prepare emergency response plans aligned with college protocols. Follow guidance provided by Le Moyne Sports Medicine and relevant departments. Music Instructor Requirement to instruct one section of MUS 395 (1-credit course) per Fall and Spring semester. All Pep Band members who are Le Moyne College students will be required to register for this course each semester of their involvement. Additional Responsibilities Maintain active and positive relationships with area high school band directors and others within the recruiting region Initial recruitment goals are 10-15 new students each fall with an annual ensemble enrollment of 30 plus students. Cultivate positive alumni and community relationships Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Master's degree in Music, Education, or a related field required. Experience leading a band or similar ensemble, preferably at the collegiate or high school level. Strong musical leadership skills. Excellent communication, organization, and interpersonal skills. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and during game-day events. Familiarity with drumline instruction and coordination, particularly in a marching or athletic band setting; ability to integrate percussion effectively into high-energy performances is strongly preferred. Additional Information: Pay Range: $15,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Occupational-Therapist-and-Community-Program-Leader_JR100347": {
      "title": "Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                         The Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader is responsible for planning, implementing, and evaluating community-based occupational therapy services that promote healthy aging, independence, and fall prevention for older adults. This position provides evidence-informed fall prevention programming, functional assessments, home safety education, and wellness interventions while collaborating with community organizations throughout Central New York. Occupational Therapist and Community Program Leader assists with program development, participant outcome measurement, data management, and community outreach to support CARE's mission of improving the health, safety, and quality of life of older adults. This is a part time position working 25 hours per week. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receival of those funds. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Occupational Therapy and Fall Prevention Conduct standardized assessments to identify fall risk, balance deficits, mobility limitations, and functional performance among older adults. Implement CARE's evidence-informed fall prevention and healthy aging programs in community settings. Develop individualized recommendations and intervention strategies to improve balance, strength, mobility, confidence, and safe participation in daily activities. Provide education on fall prevention, home safety, aging in place, adaptive strategies, and healthy aging to participants, caregivers, and community organizations. Conduct home safety evaluations and provide recommendations for environmental modifications and adaptive equipment when appropriate. Monitor participant progress and modify interventions as needed to maximize outcomes. Collaborate with healthcare professionals, senior service agencies, community organizations, and residential facilities to coordinate services and promote participant success. Assist with supervision and mentoring of occupational therapy students during fieldwork experiences, as assigned. Community Programming and Program Development Deliver group education sessions and evidence-informed exercise components that support CARE's healthy aging and fall prevention initiatives. Assist in the development, implementation, and evaluation of new occupational therapy and healthy aging programs. Collaborate with CARE staff to expand programming and strengthen partnerships throughout the community. Develop educational materials, participant resources, and program content that support healthy aging and fall prevention initiatives. Participate in community outreach events, health fairs, workshops, and presentations representing CARE and Le Moyne College. Data Management and Program Evaluation Collect, maintain, and analyze participant outcome data from CARE's fall prevention programs, ensuring accurate and timely entry into the CAMS reporting system. Prepare and submit monthly reports summarizing program outcomes, participation metrics, and performance data for the Onondaga County Office for Aging and other stakeholders. Monitor data quality and reporting compliance within the CAMS reporting system, utilizing findings to support program evaluation, continuous quality improvement, and grant reporting. Analyze program outcome data to identify trends, measure program effectiveness, and support strategic planning and funding initiatives. Develop and deliver annual presentations highlighting program outcomes, community impact, and key performance metrics to county partners, funding organizations, and prospective stakeholders. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Graduate degree in Occupational Therapy from an accredited program. Current New York State Occupational Therapy license in good standing. Experience working with older adults, community-based practice, fall prevention, health promotion, or wellness programming preferred. Experience conducting standardized assessments and interpreting participant outcomes preferred. Excellent organizational, project management, and computer skills. Excellent group facilitation, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. Comfort with basic digital tools for content sharing and creation (e.g., Canva, Instagram, Facebook, Zoom, Microsoft Office, etc.). Ability to collect, analyze, and report program outcome data using electronic reporting systems, including the CAMS reporting system. Experience preparing reports and presenting program outcomes to community partners, stakeholders, and funding organizations preferred. Ability to establish and maintain collaborative relationships with participants, caregivers, community partners, healthcare professionals, and students. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively as part of an interdisciplinary team. Enthusiasm for CARE's mission of promoting healthy aging, fall prevention, and community-based wellness. Must possess a reliable vehicle for travel throughout Central New York. Additional Information: Pay Range: $38.00 - $40.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Crime-Analyst_JR100336-1": {
      "title": "Crime Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                   The Crime Analyst will work on-site at the Syracuse Police Department Crime Analysis Center. The Center is staffed with a team of crime analysts and sworn law enforcement members who support area law enforcement agencies in their efforts to track and reduce Part I Crime. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Perform a variety of research and analytical tasks. Collect, compile, validate, interpret, and analyze data and trends using standard practices and techniques of crime and/or law enforcement intelligence analysis. Perform statistical, spatial, and/or qualitative analyses as needed, making use of standard software packages. Work on assignments that are moderately complex under direct or indirect supervision, where there is latitude for independent action and decision-making. Prepare and deliver reports and presentations of analytic results and may be subpoenaed to testify in court proceedings. Provide crime analysis and criminal intelligence support to law enforcement as they respond to, investigate, and otherwise address criminal activity. Any other relevant duties as assigned by supervisor. Flexibility to work evening/weekend shifts will be required. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in criminal justice, criminology, public administration, or a related field 0-1 year experience in the field of criminology, criminal justice research, or criminal justice policy. Strong written and verbal communication skills are essential. Communication with all police ranks as well as local, state, and federal agencies may be necessary. Knowledge of the criminal justice process. Understanding of basic social science research methods: concepts and techniques of measurement and analysis, and interpretation of results. Experience with databases, spreadsheets, statistical computing, and/or geographic information systems is desired. Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range :  $66,000 - $71,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace.  We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Analyst--Data_JR100341": {
      "title": "Senior Analyst, Data",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Senior Data Analyst for the Institutional Research department will assist leadership in implementing self-service, routine reporting through the development of standardized data management, retrieval and reporting tools, and working with the Director will assist the senior administration with strategic reporting and analytics. In addition to supporting the Director in the development of strategy and tactics for the IR office, the incumbent will coordinate and complete mandatory, periodic, and ad-hoc institutional reporting to maintain compliance with accrediting bodies, government agencies, college guidebooks, and other internal and external requesters. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Extract/collect, clean, analyze, and summarize data for internal use, external surveys (e.g. U.S. News and World Report, college guidebooks, rankings), government and agency mandated reporting (e.g. CDS, IPEDS, NYSED, NCAA), and continued accreditation (e.g. Middle States). Administrate and analyze each survey: Senior survey, Alumni survey; campus climate survey. Work with the HEDS organization on use of other student surveys, etc. Collaborate with the Director on market research for new and existing academic programs. Coordinate college offices, Information Technology, and outside vendors to envision and transform the College's processes for data management, analysis, and reporting. Collaborate across college offices including Financial Aid, Registrar, Finance and Administration, Enrollment Management, and Human Resources to collect and fulfill mandatory, periodic, and ad-hoc institutional reporting. Create and clearly summarize information to support institutional policies and planning, institution-wide assessment, program evaluation, and retention studies. Maintain the accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality of all College data and information. Embody Le Moyne's mission-based competencies of communication, leadership, collaboration, integrity, diversity, and service.   Assist with course evaluations and analysis with the Provost office. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in statistics, economics, computer science, and/or business analytics/data analytics required, Master’s degree in an analytical discipline such as the social sciences, education research, public policy, or related field preferred. 5+ years' experience progressively responsible experience in institutional research, applied analytics, data science, program evaluation, or a related quantitative field; equivalent combinations of graduate education and professional experience will be considered. A minimum of two years' experience in higher education or similar institutional setting. A strong aptitude in using data bases, query tools, etc. A strong understanding of research methodology in behavioral sciences or education measurement. In-depth knowledge of research methods in the social sciences and familiarity with intermediate to advanced multivariate statistical analysis techniques. Demonstrated ability collect/extract, clean, analyze, and summarize data, including competency with analytical software such as SAS and SPSS, Informer, and data visualization software, such as Tableau. Experience with education ERPs such as Workday and Datatel/Colleague preferred. Experience creating and clearly summarizing information for decision makers and other end users. Understanding and applied knowledge of digital transformation processes related to business process and cultural/organizational change. Demonstrated ability to work with less technically-savvy users to develop the scope of reporting, data requirements, and appropriate tools for extraction and reporting. Strong management, interpersonal skills, including active listening, flexibility, and empathy to accurately obtain information from and provide information to client offices and senior leadership. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 64,000 - $72,000 Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Student-Advocate--LPP_JR100338": {
      "title": "Student Advocate, LPP",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY The Student Advocate fosters a program environment conducive to the academic, social, and personal development of students in grades 8-12. Our goal is to help students stay in school, graduate, and plan for their future. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Partner individually with students through targeted mentorship to build self-direction and actionable paths toward future goals. Motivating students collectively and individually to achieve academic success through encouraging, advising, and planning strategies. Providing academic assistance to students including tutoring, homework assistance, and exam review in all subject areas, and assistance in standardized test preparation. Encouraging student completion and reviewing of PLP’s and SEA’s to drive individual case management. Handling other duties as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree NYS K-12 Teaching Certification preferred An interest in, and commitment to, academic achievement for high school students An understanding of and comfort with culturally diverse populations Excellent written and oral communication skills Flexibility and adaptability are essential Additional Information: Pay Range:  $18.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
