    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Head-Coach--Swimming-Diving-and-Director--Aquatics_JR100329-1": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Swimming/Diving and Director, Aquatics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Swimming and Diving Head Coach/Aquatics Director is responsible for conducting a comprehensive, high quality NCAA Division I athletic program within the guidelines of all rules and policies established by the department, the institution, the Conference, and the NCAA. This includes assessing, implementing, and evaluating strategies to enhance team and individual athletic and academic performance in accordance with the stated mission of Le Moyne College and the Athletic Department. This Head Coach is charged with creating an environment advancing the “Inside the L” culture of wholistic personal growth and development of the student-athlete. Additional responsibilities include serving as the College's Aquatic Director and management of all swimming pool activities.  Daily duties and tasks which require exercising discretion and independent judgment consisting of 50% instructional and 50% recruitment/administrative /fiscal management tasks /aquatics. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Coaching and Team Development: Assess, implement and evaluate strategies that enhances team and individual performance. Provide timely and constructive individualized feedback for student-athlete improvement. Prepare individuals and the team for competition, focused on high-level performance and sportsmanship. Sports Performance: Submit all paperwork, schedule meetings and respond to all information requests from athletic trainers and team physicians according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Head Athletic Trainer. All decisions regarding the health and safety of student athletes when it comes to physical participation is at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Coordinate with Peak Performance Team (Strength and Conditioning, Sports Medicine, Nutrition, Mental Health) on the conduct of a comprehensive training program to enhance both personal and performance growth/development. Game Management: Work with appropriate personnel to determine your needs for the organization, coordination, and scheduling of all home and away contests including:  facility and equipment set-up, officials, scorekeepers, statisticians, media considerations, lodging, meals, travel arrangements, etc. NCAA Compliance: Conduct program in compliance with all applicable NCAA, conference, and institutional policies, rules and regulations. Ensure timely submission of all compliance related work flows through ARMS to maintain the highest levels of integrity and transparency. Maintain open and responsive communications with the Athletics NCAA Compliance Department Maintain up to date certification in all required areas (NCAA DI Institute Modules, 1st Aid/CPR/AED Training, Etc). Fiscal Management: Submit all budget requests, documentation, receipts and related forms and paperwork, according to existing policy and established deadlines. Monitor all budgets as they relate to your program. Stay within budget allocations. Account for all money related to the program, including fund raising, camps, clinics and special events. Comply with College and department fiscal guidelines and policies. Strategically award and monitor all athletics grants in aid to best leverage the academic progress rating (APR). Enrollment Management/Recruiting and Retention: Assist leading and supporting the College Enrollment Management priorities through partnership, participation, and meeting goals with Enrollment Management initiatives. Identify, recruit, and retain athletically and academically talented prospective student athletes who will embrace the core values of Le Moyne College athletics . Assist the department with its gender equity planning and the satisfaction of all Title IX legislation by striving to attain goals related to any applicable enrollment management initiatives within your particular program. Promote and offer available experiential learning/internship/work study opportunities to incoming prospects and/or general students, which are developed and managed either by the department or through your program. Respond to all requests for information from prospective student-athletes, coaches, parents, and/or friends of prospective student-athletes. Solicit information from and distribute information to eligible prospective student-athletes and coaches and or parents or friends of prospective student-athletes. Develop and distribute appropriate recruiting materials, publications and information to interested prospective student-athletes. Follow up with appropriate offers of scholarships in a timely manner. Maintain accurate and comprehensive recruiting records of all prospective student athletes. Academic Support: Provide the appropriate academic support, assistance, motivation and environment for student-athletes. Maintain familiarity with appropriate academic resource and assistance programs available to student-athletes. Monitor the academic progress of your student-athletes from current class work to graduation. Promote the importance of academic achievement and life skills development College and Department Service: It is expected that employees have a willingness and commitment to be broadly engaged and in service to the College as demonstrated through participation on committees and attendance at College functions/events. It is expected that employees participate with department committees, as elected or assigned, to develop, evaluate and enhance department policy. Attendance at all departmental meetings, unless excused in advance by the Athletic Director/AVP, is expected while a commitment to the College's priorities and the department's goals and objectives are vital to the success of the position. It is expected that employees complete all online educational and training modules required by the College (Cybersecurity training, Title IX/Diversity & Inclusion training, etc). It is expected that employees are fully committed and engaged in advancing the department’s “Inside the L” culture. Sports Information: Respond to all information requests and work with the media, etc. according to guidelines and deadlines established by Athletic Communications. Always inform Athletic Communications when you or any of your athletes has been contacted by the media. Fund Raising Head Coaches are expected to fully understand and support the College's policies and procedures, along with any departmental guidelines, for all fund-raising activities. Expectation to secure a minimum 10% of your programmatic budget through individual giving or grants. Accountable for driving fundraising initiatives to support strategic goals not funded through programmatic budget. Responsible for cultivating donor relationships and meeting annual development targets. Particular attention should be given to NCAA legislation surrounding NIL, booster groups and donors. Reconciliation of all revenues and deposits should be handled in accordance with institutional and departmental policy. Head Coaches are expected to fully support the Dolphin Athletic Association and its programming to engage key stakeholder groups of their respective program such as alumni and families/friends. Community Service: A commitment to community services is an important tenant of the College's mission and to that end it is anticipated that employees will be involved in various community activities as a representative of the Le Moyne College Athletics Department. Identify and cultivate a community partnership with a service-based organization to provide an impactful service experience for your student-athletes. Supervision and Evaluation of Assistant Coaches by Head Coaches: Head Coaches are responsible for the supervision and evaluation of each assistant coach involved with your program. A successful head coach will keep assistant coaches informed of all applicable rules, regulations, deadlines, meetings and/or other policies. All staff members (including volunteers) must satisfy the hiring guidelines of the Department prior to assuming their respective duties, and must pass the NCAA Division I Modules each year. Aquatic Director: Scheduling and staffing of all pool functions, activities and events including but not limited to college recreation program opportunities, varsity athletics, camps/clinics, and external events/rentals Development and coordination of a comprehensive pool maintenance program which includes cleaning, water chemistry, mechanical upkeep, equipment checks and chemical inventory.  In addition, work in conjunction with Building and Grounds. Hiring, staffing and supervision of lifeguards. Maintenance of pool safety equipment. Professional Development: Opportunities to maintain and advance current understandings of techniques, strategies, theories, and regulations as they relate to the athletics industry are essential. Attendance and participation in conferences is strongly encouraged. Supervisory Relationships: For purpose of performance evaluations and most other official duties, the first level of contact for the Head Coach is with Sports Administrator. Appeals of decisions are to be taken to the Athletics Director/AVP. Functional Relationships/Secondary Sources: All coaches are expected to work cooperatively with all members of the Athletic Department (Administrators, Support Staff, Colleagues), and any other campus (admissions, housing, financial aid, maintenance, etc), or community office/agency that you might be involved with. Communications and required documentation should be handled in a timely manner.   Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications   Bachelor's degree required, Master's degree highly desirable. 3 to 5 years of progressive experience in the conduct of a collegiate level swimming program with proven success in recruiting high quality student athletes and/or equivalent related experiences. Knowledge of and ability to apply NCAA and conference rules as they pertain to the men's and women's swimming programs. The successful candidate will be required to be First Aid/CPR/AED certified and to complete all required NCAA DI Institute modules prior to being able to participate in off campus recruiting activities and countable athletically related activities. Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills needed. Certificates for Certified Pool Operator, Lifeguard/CPR/AED, and Water Safety Instructor. Preferred certificates in Lifeguard Instructor and Instructor Trainer as well as professional certifications with the College Swim Coaches Association of America and/or the American Swim Coaches Association. Preferred Aquatic Director experience.  Must possess a valid, current U.S. driver’s license. Must have reliable transportation or the ability to rent a vehicle when needed to travel to recruiting sites. May need to drive campus vehicles for local events Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $58,000 - $70,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Security-Officer--4pm-12am_JR100334": {
      "title": "Security Officer, 4pm-12am",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Job Description: Security Officers are tasked with the general responsibility of the safety and security of the Le Moyne College Campus and Le Moyne College Community. They are service driven and provide both general and emergency public safety/security services. Job duties specific to this position:   Conduct patrols of the campus, which can be walking, fixed post or by vehicle. Provide security services to specific areas of campus as assigned.  Develop and improve working relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Perform some traditional law enforcement duties typically assigned to security personnel.  Respond promptly and professionally to requests for service from students, employees and visitors for emergencies and general security services on campus. Enforce Le Moyne College's rules, regulations and policies. Ensure local, state and federal laws and ordinances are enforced to protect students, faculty/staff and visitors to the campus. Conduct thorough security checks of your assigned areas and report any security or safety issues which could lead to injury or safety concerns in order to ensure their integrity and the safety of their inhabitants and contents.  As assigned - conduct investigations and inquiry into incidents involving violations of College policy, criminal offenses or suspicious circumstances. Submit comprehensive written reports on all such incidents.  Promptly correct and/or report to the appropriate College office all observed safety, security, utility, environmental and fire hazards.  Lock and unlock buildings and rooms as scheduled.  Provide unlocks and lock-ups as requested (i.e., student key ins, office key ins). Conduct monthly inspections of fire extinguishers located on campus.  Stay well informed on all College activity.  Promote crime prevention and fire safety. Maintain a professional appearance to include uniforms, vehicles and personal hygiene. Maintain a level of physical fitness necessary to perform the principle job functions. Perform all related security services or emergency/general duties as requested by the Director of Security or his designee. Maintain a lost and found property. Cover the dispatch desk and duties when assigned. Participate in all required and assigned trainings. Work events as assigned. Test Blue light phones. Provide various forms of transports/escorts. Conduct fire drills. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne's mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college's strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne's established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Requirements: High School Diploma or GED Valid New York State driver's license and a driving record which is aligned with the College's motor vehicle policy Meet and maintain the requirements and training to be licensed and registered as a security guard in New York State. Capable of working evenings, nights, weekends, holidays and in inclement weather. Must be able and willing to work overtime coverage when necessary or directed, including mandatory overtime and for extracurricular campus events.  Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent customer service skills The ability to interact in a sensitive, courteous and understanding way with members of a diverse residential and academic community and the general public.  Ability to multi task and to maintain composure in emergency situations.   Ability to respond to calls for service.  Be reliable and able to work independently.  Must exercise good judgment and display sensitivity to the unique role that security plays in a college setting. Able to perform the physical duties of the job including, but not limited to, climbing stairs, crouching, walking, standing, or sitting for extended periods.  Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range : $26.30 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace.  We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Security-Officer--4pm-12am_JR100335": {
      "title": "Security Officer, 4pm-12am",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer and encourages women, persons of color, and Jesuits to apply for employment. Job Description: Security Officers are tasked with the general responsibility of the safety and security of the Le Moyne College Campus and Le Moyne College Community. They are service driven and provide both general and emergency public safety/security services. Job duties specific to this position:   Conduct patrols of the campus, which can be walking, fixed post or by vehicle. Provide security services to specific areas of campus as assigned.  Develop and improve working relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Perform some traditional law enforcement duties typically assigned to security personnel.  Respond promptly and professionally to requests for service from students, employees and visitors for emergencies and general security services on campus. Enforce Le Moyne College's rules, regulations and policies. Ensure local, state and federal laws and ordinances are enforced to protect students, faculty/staff and visitors to the campus. Conduct thorough security checks of your assigned areas and report any security or safety issues which could lead to injury or safety concerns in order to ensure their integrity and the safety of their inhabitants and contents.  As assigned - conduct investigations and inquiry into incidents involving violations of College policy, criminal offenses or suspicious circumstances. Submit comprehensive written reports on all such incidents.  Promptly correct and/or report to the appropriate College office all observed safety, security, utility, environmental and fire hazards.  Lock and unlock buildings and rooms as scheduled.  Provide unlocks and lock-ups as requested (i.e., student key ins, office key ins). Conduct monthly inspections of fire extinguishers located on campus.  Stay well informed on all College activity.  Promote crime prevention and fire safety. Maintain a professional appearance to include uniforms, vehicles and personal hygiene. Maintain a level of physical fitness necessary to perform the principle job functions. Perform all related security services or emergency/general duties as requested by the Director of Security or his designee. Maintain a lost and found property. Cover the dispatch desk and duties when assigned. Participate in all required and assigned trainings. Work events as assigned. Test Blue light phones. Provide various forms of transports/escorts. Conduct fire drills. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne's mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college's strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne's established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Requirements: High School Diploma or GED Valid New York State driver's license and a driving record which is aligned with the College's motor vehicle policy Meet and maintain the requirements and training to be licensed and registered as a security guard in New York State. Capable of working evenings, nights, weekends, holidays and in inclement weather. Must be able and willing to work overtime coverage when necessary or directed, including mandatory overtime and for extracurricular campus events.  Strong written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent customer service skills The ability to interact in a sensitive, courteous and understanding way with members of a diverse residential and academic community and the general public.  Ability to multi task and to maintain composure in emergency situations.   Ability to respond to calls for service.  Be reliable and able to work independently.  Must exercise good judgment and display sensitivity to the unique role that security plays in a college setting. Able to perform the physical duties of the job including, but not limited to, climbing stairs, crouching, walking, standing, or sitting for extended periods.  Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range : $26.30 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College is an equal opportunity employer that is committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace.  We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Campus-Ministry--Retreat-Ministry-and-Faith-Formation_JR100330": {
      "title": "Campus Ministry, Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Campus Ministry The Office of Campus Ministry provides opportunities for students, staff, and faculty to grow spiritually, to engage in local, domestic, and international service and social justice opportunities, to make spiritual retreats, reflect on contemporary social issues and to actively practice their faith. Campus Ministry welcomes and serves persons of all religious affiliations and faith traditions. Position Summary                                                                            Under the supervision of the Director of The Grace Center for Faith and Community and in collaboration with the Campus Ministry Staff, the Campus Minister for Retreat Ministry and Faith Formation promotes the deepening of an active faith and spiritual life, personal and communal, among the students of Le Moyne College. The primary ministry is to create vibrant programing, robust retreat offerings, individual and communal prayer/discernment opportunities, and community centered activities that help deepen, renew, or begin a personal relationship with God. This work is accomplished through a strong understanding of Ignatian spirituality and the stages of faith formation in young adults. This position requires a person who will creatively and strategically develop new programs/mediums and refine existing programs based on the ongoing assessment of student needs and interests. This is an 11 month position that works from August through June.   Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Create a compelling vision for and develop a dynamic portfolio of retreats and other experiences which will engage students in various aspects of faith formation and spiritual development.  Implement all aspects of the retreat program and other faith formation opportunities for students based on class year (First Year Student Retreat, Senior Retreat etc.) as well as topic based (Kairos, Busy Student Retreat, Health & Wellness Retreat, Silent Retreat).  Create new retreat and faith formation opportunities for students of all faiths and for those with no religious beliefs.  Promote opportunities to learn about and practice Ignatian Spirituality.  Create and maintain assessment measures for the program.  Recruit, mentor, develop and empower student leaders who support the retreat program.      Reserve and coordinate the use of various retreat facilities and college vans. Coordinate the OCIA & Confirmation program. Work with faith and service-based student organizations. Keep and maintain accurate budget records for all programs. Maintain a respectful environment for a diverse population of students; embrace diversity in the College and greater community, and treat students as individuals. Work collaboratively with the Grace Center team and campus partners Serve, as needed, as a mentor for Campus Ministry's Service opportunities Assist with local service/outreach initiatives. Serve as a Campus Ministry presence at Sunday Mass and attend all special liturgies of the college. Attend and be visible at various religious services on campus, including but not limited to weekly Jumu'ah prayer and Protestant worship. Attending and being visible at various campus events, including but not limited to sporting, musical, lectures, and other social events. Contribute to Mission Integration divisional meetings, webinars and committees Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree preferred, Bachelor's Degree required in Pastoral Studies, theology or a related field. An understanding of the principles of Ignatian spirituality, the Spiritual Exercises of St. Ignatius, the mission of Jesuit education, and Catholic Social Teaching. Desire to work with a diverse faith community of undergraduate college students. Familiarity with Karios retreat program. Knowledge of O.C.I.A. High level of initiative and imagination. Flexibility to work extended and/or off-hours to meet program needs. Ability to relate and collaborate with various groups both within the Le Moyne College community and the larger Syracuse community. Ability to maintain confidentiality, be self-directed and motivated, possess a high energy level and positive attitude. Knowledge of computers, emphasis on Microsoft Office, Excel, Gmail and various social media platforms. Strong organization and administrative skills. Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $ 57,158 - $59,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/HVAC-Mechanic_JR100316": {
      "title": "HVAC Mechanic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary The HVAC Mechanic is responsible for the repair, maintenance, operation, adjustment and installation of heating, air conditioning, refrigeration equipment, and related control systems. Principal Duties and Essential Functions: Install, repair, adjust, service and maintain electric or pneumatic control systems for heating, ventilation, air conditioning, humidity, laboratory equipment, including calibration of related instruments, gauges and controls. Install, operate, service, and repair conventional mechanical refrigeration/air conditioning equipment including standard refrigerators, and general air conditioning units. Repair, clean, adjust, and/or install oil and gas burners and auxiliary heating specialties other than high-pressure equipment. Conduct necessary tests of equipment to determine malfunctions or causes of breakdown; remove and replace faulty parts, subassemblies and major components; re-test equipment with repaired components and make required adjustments and corrections. Recommend ordering of necessary parts and supplies for maintenance of equipment. Maintain air compressors, air dryers, and low voltage installations such as warning light systems. Instruct and advise users of proper operation of equipment. May be required to make emergency repairs at hours other than normal schedule. May direct helpers and other tradesmen in performance of duties. Calibrate gas ovens and electric grills. Install additional electrical/plumbing components to improve performance or for adaptation of existing systems. Perform duties outside classification incidental to the responsibilities of the Physical Plant Department or such duties assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications: High School diploma or equivalent. Five years minimum experience in HVAC trade with working knowledge of steam hydronic and forced air heating, refrigeration, gas electric, pneumatic and direct digital control systems. Knowledge of heating, refrigeration/air conditioning equipment and/or pneumatic and electrical control systems as applicable to work specialty. Experience with steam, hot water and chilled water systems. Provides their own tools, and knows materials, methods and hazards of trade. Skill in the use of tools of the trade. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job, including heavy lifting. Must possess a valid NYS Driver’s license. EPA certification for Refrigerant Handling. May have to work overtime hours on an intermittent basis when operational needs arise . Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  40 hour work week Pay Range:  $28.82 - $30.81 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Admission-Couselor_JR100327": {
      "title": "Senior Admission Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Admission Counselor is responsible to educate incoming freshman, transfers, parents and counselors about Le Moyne College and the overall college admission process and manage all aspects of college admission including recruitment, counseling, academic advising and evaluation of prospective students and applicants. This position is based at Le Moyne College in Syracuse, NY with a main recruitment territory of Metro NY. This position requires travel to the Metro NY area for student recruitment.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Contribute to the design, development and execution of marketing and recruitment strategies to drive enrollment growth by collaborating with the Director and admission team.  Successfully manage assigned primary, secondary and tertiary geographic territories, conducting extensive travel to build pipelines, lead recruitment events and expand institutional reach.   Counsel, advise and interview prospective first-year and transfer students to guide them through the enrollment lifecycle. Evaluate prospective students’ application materials for final recommendations on admission decisions. Engage in targeted telemarketing and outreach activities to prospective students and applicants. Assist in the coordination and execution of campus open house recruitment events. Plan and host on campus programs for specific student demographics. Maximizes opportunities regarding the college admission process and access to Le Moyne College by delivering inclusive, culturally sensitive guidance to diverse students, parents and counselors. Plans travel and recruitment in the Metro NY area: Visit high schools, junior colleges and multicultural agencies to educate students and counselors about Le Moyne College to build relationships and expand College visibility Conduct off campus interviews during recruiting trips. Engage with local alumni during travel to strengthen relationships and support local enrollment initiatives Represent Le Moyne College at organized off campus recruiting programs including, college nights, national and regional colleges, fairs and mini days. Plan, schedule, and present at Student Information Sessions in targeted geographic areas. (off-campus receptions) Plan, schedule, and present at off campus guidance counselor breakfasts, dinners and association meetings. Participate in panel presentations at secondary schools when invitations are extended to us. Coordinate or assist with other admission related events and programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited College or University required. Experience working in an admission office preferred. Valid Driver’s License required. Excellent oral, presentation and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and time management. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Flexibility and willingness to work extended hours during various time periods including evenings and weekends. High level of initiative and imagination. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish is preferred, but not required. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $24.00 - $27.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Registrar_JR100317": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Assistant Registrar is responsible for all functions within the Registrar’s Office as it relates to student records, degree completion, and curriculum management. In collaboration with other Assistant/Associate Registrars, this position will support the oversight of operations within the Registrar’s Office to ensure successful and efficient performance.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Contribute to the day-to-day operations of the Registrar’s office. Interpret and enforce Federal, State, and College policies, rules, and regulations as appropriate. Maintain data integrity of student academic records. Provide excellent customer service to the constituents of the Registrar’s Office (i.e. students, families, faculty, staff, external agencies, etc.) regarding student records. Commencement and degree completion, including but not limited to: Academic advising to support degree completion Related communications with students, faculty, and staff to support degree persistence and student success. Graduation applications, degree audits, degree conferrals, and data reporting. Collaboration with campus-wide partners to ensure the accuracy and integrity of student records data associated with commencement, honors, awards, and degree conferral activities. Processing of student hiatuses and related communications. Study abroad and international transfer credit analysis in collaboration with various administrators and offices across campus. National Clearinghouse and NSLDS enrollment reporting, degree verification, and error resolutions. Maintenance of document management and workflow solutions, including OnBase, Google forms, and related technologies. Serve as the primary liaison for student systems vendors and external partners, including National Student Clearinghouse and Parchment as well as additional technologies as needed. Assist the Registrar’s Office with: All communications to and from the Registrar’s office, including phone calls, emails, and official correspondences. Maintenance of student educational records. The identification, investigation and resolution of issues and processing errors regarding registration and records areas. Streamlining policies and procedures to improve efficiency. Evaluate, implement, and test new software, upgrades, and new systems utilized in the Registrar’s Office. Development of training materials and serve as the College’s training resource for best practices within student information systems, supportive software, reporting, and solutions for student information systems (SIS) and related software. Serve on selected college committees. Attendance at College events as needed (some evenings and weekends). Other duties as assigned. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications     Bachelor’s degree and 2-5 years of related experience in a higher education setting (experience in a Registrar’s Office is preferred). Professional demeanor and ability to interact well with others in a fast-paced operation. Strong knowledge of student records administration, academic operations, and higher education business processes. Demonstrated ability to analyze complex issues, develop practical solutions, and lead operational improvements. Strong interpersonal, leadership, communication, and organizational skills as well as proven ability to work collaboratively. Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines effectively. Attention to detail and proficiency in Excel is essential. Respect for confidential information; working knowledge of FERPA is required. Experience with Colleague Datatel, Unity OnBase, Parchment, and Informer is preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $63,300 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Admission_JR100326": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Admission",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Assistant Director is responsible to educate incoming freshman, transfers, parents and counselors about Le Moyne College and the overall college admission process and manage all aspects of college admission including recruitment, counseling, academic advising and evaluation of prospective students and applicants. This position is based at Le Moyne College in Syracuse, NY with a main recruitment territory of Metro NY. This position requires travel to the Metro NY area for student recruitment.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Participate as an active member of the professional admission team to design, develop and implement successful marketing and recruitment strategies and plans. Successfully manage assigned primary, secondary and tertiary geographic territories conducting extensive travel to build pipelines, lead recruitment events and expand institutional reach. Counsel, advise and interview prospective first-year and transfer students to guide them through the enrollment lifecycle Evaluate prospective students’ application materials for final recommendations on admission decision. Engage in targeted telemarketing and outreach activities to prospective students and applicants. Lead the organization and execution of on-campus events with the support of the Director of First Year Admission. Plan and host on campus programs for specific student demographics Maximize opportunities regarding the college admission process and access to Le Moyne College by delivering inclusive, culturally sensitive guidance to diverse students, parents and counselors Responsible for specific program responsibilities as assigned by Director (ex: travel coordination, tour guides, etc.) Build, expand, and maintain an internal recruitment database Plans travel and recruitment in the Metro NY area: Visit high schools, junior colleges and multicultural agencies to educate students and counselors about Le Moyne College to build relationships and expand College visibility Conduct off campus interviews during recruiting trips. Engage with local alumni during travel to strengthen relationships and support local enrollment initiatives Represent Le Moyne College at organized off campus recruiting programs including, college nights, national and regional colleges, fairs and mini days. Plan, schedule, and present at Student Information Sessions in targeted geographic areas. (off-campus receptions) Plan, schedule, and present at off campus guidance counselor breakfasts, dinners and association meetings. Participate in panel presentations at secondary schools when invitations are extended to us. Coordinate or assist with other admission related events and programs. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited College or University and 3 years of experience required. Experience working in an admission office preferred. Valid Driver’s License required. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. Excellent oral, presentation and written communication skills. Strong organizational skills and time management. Flexibility and willingness to work extended hours during various time periods including evenings and weekends. High level of initiative and imagination. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish is preferred, but not required. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $26.00 - $30.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Professional-Tutor--STEP_JR100314": {
      "title": "Professional Tutor, STEP",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. STEP Program The Le Moyne College Science and Technology Entry Program (STEP) is one of 51 STEP programs in New York State preparing economically disadvantaged students from Nottingham High School, Henninger High School, Syracuse Middle Schools and all of Onondaga County for college. Collaborating with the New York State Department of Education and the Syracuse City School District since 1987, we’re proud of our students’ pursuit of careers in math, science, technology and the health-related or licensed professions. Position Summary  The professional tutor is a vital link between our STEP students (grades 8th – 12th in the Syracuse City School District) and other professional staff within the program. The professional tutor functions as a student advocate and role model and assists program participants to achieve both academic and professional success. This is a part-time position for 2-3 Saturdays per month from 9am-1:30pm. There are a total of 21 Saturdays over the academic school year. This position is funded by external sources and is contingent on the continued receival of those funds.  Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position:  Perform one-on-one meetings with students in the program to assist with short and long-range educational goals. Provide academic and professional counseling including assistance with college application process and employment applications; and identify students who require additional academic support services. Facilitate seminars and programming with the assistance of other STEP professionals that contribute to the goal of advancing student's academic, personal, and professional growth. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree required, Science majors preferred (biology, chemistry, or related) NYS Teaching certificate preferred.  An interest in, and commitment to, high school students. Commitment to, and comfort with, culturally diverse populations. Excellent communication skills required. This is a position includes 2-3 Saturdays per month (21 over the academic year) Flexibility and adaptability are essential. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $20.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Senior-Associate-Athletic-Director--External-Affairs_JR100310": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Athletic Director, External Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Sr. Associate Athletic Director for External Affairs is a key member of the Athletic leadership team, responsible for the strategic vision, oversight, and execution of all external units within Le Moyne College Athletics. This role is directly accountable for driving departmental revenue, elevating the game-day fan experience, and modernizing sports information and digital media strategies. By unifying corporate partnerships, ticket operations, marketing, and media relations, the Sr. Associate AD ensures a seamless, high-energy fan experience that builds institutional visibility, engages the campus and local communities, and converts fan affinity into long-term financial stability. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Revenue Generation & Strategic Planning (30%) Provide oversight for the identification, solicitation, and closure of new corporate sponsorship agreements Oversee the management of existing partner relationships, ensuring complete contract fulfillment, in-game asset delivery, and multi-year renewals. Provide strategic oversight for the ticket office. Develop and execute aggressive strategies for season, group, mini-plan, and single-game ticket packages to maximize venue capacity and optimize revenue. Explore and establish targets for alternative revenue opportunities, including premium seating, hospitality experiences, merchandise licensing, and digital content monetization. Utilize data analytics and market research to provide regular revenue forecasting, attendance metrics, and strategic performance analysis to the Athletic Director/AVP. Fan Experience & Game Atmosphere Production (30%) Own the overall atmosphere of all home sporting events to ensure a vibrant home-court advantage. Direct and approve all in-game creative elements, music, public address scripts, video board content, and promotional activations. Lead and coordinate game-day stakeholders—including the pep band, cheer/dance squads, spirit groups, and third-party game staff—to maintain a professional, high-energy environment. Collaborate with campus partners to design and execute innovative theme nights, giveaways, and community relations initiatives to increase attendance among students, faculty, staff, and the broader Central New York public. Sports Information, Communications & Brand Development (30%) Oversee and actively contribute to the sports information and communications unit. Direct strategies to build positive relationships with local, regional, and national media to generate national storytelling opportunities. Supervise the coordination of content for the official athletics website and all social media platforms. Establish strict proofing and layer-of-approval processes for public-facing digital materials to ensure strict alignment with college brand standards. Ensure the accurate production of all sports media guides, historical archiving, and live game-day statistics operations. Leadership, Sport Administration & Compliance (10%) Serve on the Athletic Director/AVP’s senior staff, actively contributing to department-wide strategic planning and decision-making. Serve as the designated Sport Administrator for selected athletic programs, providing operational guidance and evaluating head coaches. Maintain strict adherence to and up-to-date knowledge of all NCAA Division I, conference, and institutional rules, regulations, and deadlines. Ensure the physical, emotional, and social welfare of all student-athletes. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Business, Communications, or a related field required; Master’s degree preferred. 7+ years of progressive, full-time experience in sports marketing, revenue generation, or athletic communications, preferably within NCAA Division I athletics. Proven track record of leading, managing, and developing a diverse staff of department area heads, graduate assistants, and interns. Ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally in both written and verbal forms. Proven ability to work constructively and collaboratively within a team environment and across diverse departments. Strong critical thinking skills with the ability to identify issues, propose solutions, and adapt to changing workplace needs. Commitment to fostering an inclusive, respectful, and equitable environment for all colleagues, clients, and stakeholders Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks effectively, and manage multiple projects simultaneously Demonstrated commitment to ethical conduct, honesty, and professional integrity in all workplace interactions Must possess a valid, current U.S. driver’s license. Must have reliable transportation or the ability to rent a vehicle when needed to travel. May need to drive campus vehicles for local events. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Director--Alumni-and-Donor-Relations_JR100311": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Alumni and Donor Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Director for Alumni and Donor Relations plays a vital role in planning and executing signature alumni and donor events, with primary responsibility for the logistics of Reunion Weekend and annual fundraising dinners. In addition, this position assists with athletic alumni programming, manages a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects and supports the daily administrative operations of the Alumni and Donor Relations team. The role requires excellent organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to collaborate effectively with colleagues, volunteers, and vendors to deliver high-quality experiences that strengthen connections and inspire philanthropy. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Event Management (Primary Focus) Serve as the lead project manager for Reunion Weekends, overseeing logistics, vendor coordination, volunteer support, and event communications. Plan and execute annual fundraising dinners, coordinating with Advancement, Facilities, Catering, and external vendors to deliver high-caliber donor experiences. Assist in the planning and execution of athletic alumni events, working closely with colleagues in Athletics and Advancement. Support other alumni and donor events as needed, including regional gatherings, networking programs, and recognition events. Alumni and Donor Engagement Build strong relationships with alumni volunteers, reunion committees, and event participants. Carry a small portfolio of corporate and individual prospects, engaging them through personalized outreach, event invitations, and stewardship. Assist with donor recognition activities connected to events, including program booklets, signage, and acknowledgments. Team and Administrative Support Provide day-to-day administrative support for the Alumni and Donor Relations team, including budget tracking, event registration management, and database updates. Serve as the point of contact for vendors, alumni inquiries, and internal partners related to event logistics. Contribute to Advancement communications, including event promotions, email campaigns, and website updates Collaboration Partner with colleagues across Advancement and the College to ensure events and engagement initiatives align with institutional priorities. Represent the College at alumni, donor, and campus events, occasionally requiring evening or weekend work. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 3+years of experience in event planning, alumni relations, donor relations, or related fields. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple complex events simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong relationship-building skills with alumni, donors, and volunteers. Proficiency with Microsoft Office; experience with event management platforms and advancement databases (e.g., Raiser’s Edge) preferred. Flexibility to work evenings, weekends, and travel for events as needed. Commitment to the College’s Jesuit values of service, excellence, and cura personalis (care for the whole person). Ability to occasional work evenings and weekends. Ability to travel to support alumni and donor events as needed. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $25.00 - $27.50 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Assistant-Coach--Tennis_JR100260": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Tennis",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Assistant Coach for Men’s and Women’s Tennis is responsible for providing assistance and support for the conduct of a comprehensive, high quality NCAA Division I men’s and women’s tennis program, within the guidelines of all rules and policies established by the department, the institution, the NEC Conference, and the NCAA, in accordance with the academic standards, and the stated mission of Le Moyne College and the Athletic Department, including the advancement of its “Inside the L“ shared culture. This position will require daily and/or weekly duties and tasks as assigned by the head coach which require exercising discretion and independent judgment consisting of 75% instructional and 25% recruitment/administrative activities. This is a ten month position from August 1st through May 31st. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: NCAA Compliance Assist program in compliance with all applicable NCAA, conference, and institutional policies, rules and regulations. Assist with timely submission of all compliance related work flows through Teamworks to maintain the highest levels of integrity and transparency. Maintain open and responsive communications with the Associate Director of Compliance Maintain up to date certification in all required areas (NCAA DI Institute Modules, 1st Aid/CPR/AED Training, Etc). Fiscal Management Assist with all budget requests, documentation, receipts and related forms and paperwork, according to existing policy and established deadlines as assigned by head coach. Enrollment Management Assist leading and supporting the College Enrollment Management priorities through partnership, participation, and meeting goals with Enrollment Management initiatives as assigned by head coach. Assist the department with its gender equity planning and the satisfaction of all Title IX legislation by striving to attain goals related to any applicable enrollment management initiatives within your particular program as assigned by head coach. Assist head coach with responding to all requests for information from prospective student-athletes, coaches, parents, and/or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with solicit information from and distribute information to eligible prospective student-athletes and coaches and or parents or friends of prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with developing and distributing appropriate recruiting materials, publications and information to interested prospective student-athletes. Assist head coach with maintaining accurate and comprehensive recruiting records of all prospective student athletes. College and Department Service It is expected that employees have a willingness and commitment to be broadly engaged and in service to the College as demonstrated through participation on committees and attendance at College functions/events. It is expected that employees participate with department committees, as elected or assigned, to develop, evaluate and enhance department policy. Attendance at all departmental meetings, unless excused in advance by the AVP for Athletics, is expected while a commitment to the College's priorities and the department's goals and objectives are vital to the success of the position. Academic Support Assist head coach with providing the appropriate academic support, assistance, motivation and environment for student-athletes. Become familiar with appropriate academic resource and assistance programs available to student-athletes. Assist head coach with monitoring the academic progress of your student-athletes from current class work to graduation. Understand current institutional academic standards and policies. Game Management Assist head coach with working with appropriate personnel to determine your needs for the organization, coordination, and scheduling of all home and away contests including:  facility and equipment set-up, officials, scorekeepers, statisticians, media considerations, lodging, meals, travel arrangements, etc. Sports Performance Submit all paperwork, schedule meetings and respond to all information requests from athletic trainers and team physicians according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Head Athletic Trainer as assigned by head coach. All decisions regarding the health and safety of student athletes when it comes to physical participation is at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Assist head coach with coordinating with Head Strength/Conditioning Coach on the conduct of a comprehensive training program to enhance both personal and performance growth/development. Sports Information Respond to all information requests and work with the media, etc. according to guidelines and deadlines established by the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications as assigned by head coach. Always inform the Assistant Athletic Director for Athletic Communications when you or any of your athletes has been contacted by the media. Fund Raising Assist head coach with fund raising activities. Particular attention should be given to NCAA legislation surrounding booster groups and donors. Reconciliation of all revenues and deposits should be handled in accordance with institutional and departmental policy. Community Service A commitment to community services is an important tenant of the College's mission and to that end it is anticipated that employees will be involved in various community activities as a representative of the Le Moyne College Athletics Department. Assist head coach with identifying and cultivating a community partnership with a service-based organization to provide an impactful service experience for your student-athletes. Professional Development Opportunities to maintain and advance current understandings of techniques, strategies, theories, and regulations as they relate to the athletics industry are essential. Attendance and participation in conferences is strongly encouraged if assigned by head coach. Supervisory Relationships For purpose of performance evaluations and most other official duties, the first level of contact for the Assistant Coach is with the Head Coach. Appeals of decisions are to be taken to the Director of Athletics. Functional Relationships/Secondary Sources: All coaches are expected to work cooperatively with all members of the Athletic Department (Administrators, Support Staff, Colleagues), and any other campus (admissions, housing, financial aid, maintenance, etc), or community office/agency that you might be involved with. Communications and required documentation should be handled in a timely manner. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned.      QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree preferred. 1 to 2 years of progressive experience in the conduct of a collegiate level tennis program with proven success in recruiting high quality student athletes and/or equivalent related experiences. Knowledge of and ability to apply NCAA and NEC conference rules as they pertain to tennis programs. The successful candidate will be required to be First Aid/CPR/AED certified and to complete all required NCAA DI recruiting education modules prior to being able to participate in off campus recruiting activities and countable athletically related activities. Excellent leadership, organizational, interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills needed. Additional Information: Pay Range:  $17,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Vice-President--Enrollment-Management-and-Marketing_JR100294": {
      "title": "Vice President, Enrollment Management and Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLe Moyne College, a Catholic and Jesuit college located on a 160‑acre suburban campus known as “the Heights” in Syracuse, New York, seeks nominations and applications for its next Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing . Rooted in the Jesuit tradition of cura personalis —care for the whole person—Le Moyne brings together students of all backgrounds in an inclusive, mission‑driven community focused on academic excellence and real-world impact. The College is recognized for its close-knit learning environment, highlighted by a 12:1 student‑to‑faculty ratio, small classes, and faculty who prioritize mentorship and student development. Consistently ranked among the top regional universities in the Northeast, Le Moyne combines rigorous academics across the liberal arts, sciences, business, health professions, and education with strong career preparation outcomes. At Le Moyne, there is a palpable sense of momentum and transformation shaping the institution. The College is investing boldly in its future through expanded academic programs, new partnerships, and significant campus enhancements designed to deepen student learning and engagement. Recent developments include the launch of new programs aligned with emerging fields, major state and philanthropic investments supporting health care and STEM education, and hands‑on research opportunities that allow students to work alongside faculty in nationally and globally relevant settings. At the same time, Le Moyne is reimagining its physical campus with new and renovated spaces that foster collaboration, creativity, and community, alongside the transition to Division I athletics in 2023—an important milestone that is strengthening institutional visibility and school spirit. Together, these initiatives reflect a college on the rise, confidently advancing its Jesuit mission while creating new pathways for student success and impact. The College seeks an accomplished and visionary Vice President for Enrollment Management and Marketing, who will report directly to President Linda LeMura and: Collaborate with senior leadership across the College. Lead institution-wide enrollment and marketing and serve as a key member of the President’s Leadership Team. Provide strategic and operational leadership for a comprehensive, data-informed enrollment management strategy that advances Le Moyne’s Jesuit mission, academic excellence, financial vitality, and commitment to access and diversity. Oversee undergraduate and graduate admission, financial aid, and communications and marketing. Guide integrated recruitment, retention, branding, and pricing strategies that strengthen enrollment outcomes and institutional reputation. Inspire and develop a high-performing, student-centered team. Leverage analytics and market insights to inform decision-making and optimize institutional resources. Serve as a visible advocate for Le Moyne with prospective students, families, school counselors, and external partners. Bring the vision, judgment, and energy to help shape Le Moyne’s continued momentum and future growth in a collaborative, mission-driven environment. Mission and Vision At Le Moyne College, Jesuit and Catholic values shape everything the institution does, from how it teaches to how members of the community care for one another. Its mission is grounded in cura personalis , the Jesuit principle of caring for the whole person. In practice, this means small classes where students are known by name, faculty who serve as mentors, and an emphasis on service, justice, and lifelong learning. Le Moyne supports students’ growth not only academically, but also personally and ethically, preparing them to lead meaningful lives and make a difference in the world. All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as separate documents, a CV/resume and a letter of interest. Review of applications has begun and will continue until the position is filled. For fullest consideration, all materials should be received by July 10, 2026 . Please direct all inquiries to Kim Migoya ( kmigoya@wittkieffer.com ). All nominations and applications should be submitted to Amy Crutchfield, Christy Pratt, and Kim Migoya through the WittKieffer Candidate Portal by clicking here . Candidates can also find the portal via the WittKieffer website at www.wittkieffer.com . Le Moyne College estimates the salary range for this position at $200, 000 to $220,000. The College also offers a comprehensive, competitive benefits program. Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship. Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time."
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Programmer-Analyst_JR100283": {
      "title": "Programmer Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. Position Summary                                                                            The Programmer/Analyst is central to maintaining and modernizing the College’s core administrative systems. This position is responsible for the performance, stability, and evolution of our Ellucian Colleague environment while helping transition legacy processes into scalable, modern solutions. The Programmer/Analyst acts as a technical bridge between established systems and emerging technologies—building integrations, reducing technical debt, and enabling more efficient, data-driven operations across the institution. Principal Duties and Essential Functions Job duties specific to this position: Maintain and enhance the Ellucian Colleague system and UniData environment to ensure reliability, performance, and data integrity Diagnose and resolve system issues; proactively tune and optimize system performance Develop, modify, and support applications using UniBasic and Envision Create and maintain clear, usable documentation for legacy systems and processes Safeguard sensitive institutional data in alignment with security and compliance standards Reduce technical debt by auditing and streamlining legacy custom code Identify opportunities to replace custom solutions with standard (“baseline”) system functionality Simplify and modernize system architecture to improve maintainability and scalability Decommission obsolete processes, reports, and data structures to support future system upgrades or migrations Design and implement integrations between Colleague and modern platforms (e.g., Canvas, Workday) using APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON Develop reports and data solutions using tools like SQL Server Reporting Services and Informer Support data exchange processes that enable accurate, timely reporting and decision-making across departments Partner with departments such as Financial Aid, Registrar, and Bursar to align business processes with system capabilities Translate functional needs into technical solutions within the Colleague environment Guide stakeholders through changes that reduce reliance on custom development and improve long-term sustainability Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent experience required 5+ years of programming experience, ideally in ERP or enterprise systems required Experience with SQL Server or similar relational databases required, experience with Ellucian Colleague, UniData, or UniBasic preferred Familiarity with APIs, web services (REST/SOAP), and JSON required Strong problem-solving skills and ability to translate business requirements into technical solutions Experience with reporting tools such as Informer or SQL Server Reporting Services preferred Familiarity with systems such as Canvas or Workday preferred Experience in higher education or similarly complex institutional environments preferred Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range: $70,000 - $75,000 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Student-Success_JR100257": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Student Success",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of the Student Success Center plays a pivotal role in managing the daily operations of the Center and provides professional support to all Center staff, including professionals and student employees. This position coordinates the tutoring program, collaborates closely with colleagues in the Quantitative Research Center and Writing Center, and empowers students to achieve their academic, personal, and professional goals through individualized coaching and resource connection. In addition, the Associate Director leads and supports retention initiatives by identifying enrollment and persistence risks, coordinating proactive outreach efforts, and collaborating with campus partners to strengthen student retention across all class years. This position will commence no earlier than June 1, 2026. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Center Operations/Management - 30% Oversee the Center’s daily operations such as student programming, academic support services and triage Coordinate programming efforts to support students and create visibility for the Center  Partner with colleagues to develop and implement student success initiatives Respond to inquiries from students, families, faculty, and other college personnel Promote the Center’s resources and achievements to external audiences Work collaboratively with coaches to carry out the mission, goals and outcomes of the Student Success Center Provide staff development, including hiring, mentoring, and evaluation of student staff Carry out logistical duties to support academic advising such as compiling administrative withdrawal data, sending hiatus letters, and reaching out to faculty advisors to provide support Promote and contribute to existing student success efforts while assessing their effectiveness and implementing new initiatives Case Management/Academic Coaching - 25% Provide comprehensive academic coaching to a caseload of students who have been referred. (Referrals may come from Student of Concern reports, faculty referrals, assignments based on academic standing, student-initiated requests, etc.) Engage in initiative-taking management of caseload, including consistent and direct contact with students, and targeted outreach at key points in the semester. Troubleshoot registration, billing and financial aid issues that may arise for students. Assess learner needs in order to help them make fully informed decisions about their pathways as well as challenging them to make progress toward their goals. Develop relationships with identified students that encourage continuation of long-term academic coaching into future semesters, as needed. Assist students in developing self-efficacy by identifying and overcoming obstacles that may be impeding academic success; work with students to learn strong time management and organization skills; motivate students to practice self-regulation and take ownership of their academic success. Engage at-risk students, providing one-on-one intrusive advising meetings to improve engagement and ensure success. Connect students with other campus resources related to tutoring, spiritual support, disability services, counseling and health, housing and food insecurity, career planning, finances, etc. Partner with faculty, academic advisors, and campus colleagues regarding Student of Concern referrals. Assist instructors with follow-up on students who have been referred through the Student of Concern process for excessive absences, unsatisfactory grades, etc. Record applicable interventions via Maxient. Retention Leadership – 20% Monitor early alerts, absences, GPA risk factors, DFW rates, and withdrawal patterns to identify students who may be at risk for attrition. Coordinate campus-wide retention initiatives in partnership with the Director of Student Success and other stakeholders (Dean Restaurant Nights, Registration Fest, Winter and Summer Academic Bridge). Compile the academic standing data (students on warning/probation) and notify undergraduates each semester when they are not in good academic standing Continually refine programing to support students on probation, assign counselors to support them, and provide ongoing training to counselors Lead targeted persistence campaigns focusing on key transition points (e.g., first-year to sophomore retention, post-hiatus return, students on academic warning/probation). Analyze retention and persistence trends to inform programming, resource allocation, and interventions. Collaborate with Academic Deans, Class Deans, Enrollment Management, Financial Aid, Housing, Athletics, and other departments to ensure coordinated outreach and resolution of barriers to persistence. Serve as the Student Success representative on the retention committee Implement best practices for holistic retention support that address academic, social, financial, and wellbeing risk factors. Contribute retention data insights during departmental and campus-wide meetings. Tutoring Oversight - 15% Organize the hiring, supervision, and regular training of student tutors Oversee tutor payroll and monitor the associated budget Coordinate the administration of study groups that are offered in collaboration with various departments and learning communities, including hiring, training, and payroll for peer leaders, and maintaining records on all group sessions/workshops Continually seek faculty input on tutoring effectiveness and operations Serve as a liaison to other Le Moyne College programs (i.e., the Physician Assistant program, nursing partnerships, etc.) regarding academic support issues and scheduling Maintain tutoring data and provide regular reports and assessments Professional Development - 5% Meet regularly with the Director of Student Success to discuss the status of retention data/efforts. Participate as an active member of the Student Success Center staff meetings and retreats and provide informed feedback and initiative. Serve as a member of key campus committees related to student success Attend division- and campus-wide meetings to keep current on college initiatives, student demographics, program offerings, upcoming trends, etc. Continually review best practices related to student success and relay pertinent information to campus partners as needed. Manage confidential student information with tact, discretion, and in compliance with FERPA regulations Progress Monitoring – 5% Develop and maintain accurate, organized, and detailed student records of students who have sought assistance. Create and maintain student plans in close collaboration with the Director of the Student Success Center to ensure accurate counseling, mitigation of student issues, and ongoing feedback; adjust strategies as needed. Monitor student academic progress by compiling, analyzing, and reporting on student progress utilizing available databases and resources (e.g., Phinfo, Datatel, Informer, WCOnline, CampusGroups) Assess student attrition risk and vulnerability and intervene at critical points of the student's educational path. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree and 5+ years of relevant experience is required or equivalent experience and education. Master’s degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Education or related field is preferred. Establish and maintain cooperative and productive relationships with both campus and off-campus contacts, including students, faculty, prospects, parents, and community partners Possess excellent interpersonal and written communication skills Maintain a high level of confidentiality due to the sensitivity of the nature of the student and college information this position requires Experience working directly with college students, preferably with transfer, non-traditional, and/or under-represented student populations, concerning academic success Experience with large- and small-scale event planning Experience with Microsoft Office, Datatel Student Management Software, and familiarity with Course Management Software (e.g. Canvas), Informer, and Slate are preferred Willingness to work evenings and weekends to accommodate student needs and programming Demonstrated ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment Excellent customer service skills Strong written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated time management and organization skills. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $62,354 - $66,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Associate-Director--Annual-Giving_JR100254": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Annual Giving",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Associate Director of Annual Giving plays a key role in the planning, execution, and management of strategies that drive philanthropic support through annual giving programs. This position focuses on donor acquisition, retention, and upgrading, as well as strengthening engagement among alumni, parents, faculty, staff, and friends of the College. The Associate Director partners closely with colleagues in Advancement, particularly with the Engagement Center, and Marketing and Communications to design multi-channel campaigns that inspire giving and align with institutional priorities. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Support the development and implementation of a comprehensive annual giving plan to achieve participation and revenue goals. Oversee key components of the annual giving program, including direct mail, email, texting, digital campaigns, crowdfunding, and Giving Day. Review giving data and trends to inform segmentation, messaging, and campaign strategies. Collaborate with the Advancement team to identify new opportunities for donor engagement and pipeline growth. Manage a portfolio of annual donors and prospects to cultivate, solicit, and steward gifts Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations to ensure execution of stewardship plans that recognize annual giving donors at all levels. Partner with Alumni and Donor Relations team to integrate giving opportunities into campus and regional events. Supervise and mentor staff, students, and/or volunteers engaged in annual giving efforts. Collaborate across Advancement to ensure consistency and coordination in fundraising messages and donor experiences. Track and report on campaign performance, donor retention, participation rates, and other key metrics. Maintain accurate records in the Raiser’s Edge and GiveCampus CRM systems. Use data to identify trends, test new strategies, and inform long-term planning. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree required. 5+ years of experience in fundraising, annual giving, or related field required, experience in higher education preferred. Demonstrated success managing campaigns or projects from conception through completion. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong analytical skills with experience using data to drive decisions. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent customer service skills. Ability to work independently but collaboratively as part of a goal-oriented team. Commitment to the Jesuit mission and values of the College. Familiarity with CRM systems and fundraising software (e.g., Raiser’s Edge, GiveCampus) preferred. Understanding of donor segmentation and digital fundraising techniques preferred. Supervisory and/or volunteer management experience preferred. Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  35 hour work week Pay Range:  $63,000 - $73,500 annually Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
    },
    "https://agilitas.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/LMC/job/Syracuse-NY/Administrator--Desktop-Systems_JR100252": {
      "title": "Administrator, Desktop Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout Le Moyne College: Le Moyne College, located in Syracuse, N.Y., is an independent college established by the Jesuits in 1946 to provide students with a values-based, comprehensive academic program designed to foster intellectual excellence and preparation for a life of leadership and service. Today, Le Moyne has evolved into a nationally acclaimed college of liberal arts and sciences that draws students from across the U.S. and abroad. Our Mission: Le Moyne College is a diverse learning community that strives for academic excellence in the Catholic and Jesuit tradition through its comprehensive programs rooted in the liberal arts and sciences. Its emphasis is on education of the whole person and on the search for meaning and value as integral parts of the intellectual life. Le Moyne College seeks to prepare its members for leadership and service in their personal and professional lives to promote a more just society. Le Moyne College aims to advance the values of diversity and inclusiveness at the college. To do this, Le Moyne seeks scholars and professionals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to the campus, and who bring greater depth, breadth, and diversity to our campus community. POSITION SUMMARY                                                                      The Desktop Systems Administrator is responsible and accountable for the effective lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing devices, and academic software. This includes processes and technologies associated with acquisition, inventory and asset management, imaging and installation, configuration, maintenance, renewal and disposal of computing devices and software. The Desktop Administrator supervises and coordinates the activities of student employees who support the lifecycle management activities. Actively advances and promotes Le Moyne’s mission, Catholic and Jesuit identity, and commitment to both social justice and care for the whole person PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Job duties specific to this position: Desktop Administration Actively leads the lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing devices, including device acquisition, creation of OS image and deployment of baseline system configuration, for Windows, Apple Mac OS, Google Chromebook and Apple iOS devices. Ensures timely and consistent distribution of software updates and security patches in accordance with departmental standards. Identifies, utilizes and maintains methods and technologies to promote efficient device and software configuration management. Effectively integrates third party hardware (e.g. printers, scanners, copiers) into Le Moyne’s personal and mobile computing environment. Establishes and documents best practices for the technical support of computing and mobile devices. Evaluates and recommends devices and software to satisfy specified requirements. Serves as a consultant regarding questions involving system(s) installation, configuration, and maintenance. Application Administration Actively leads the end to end lifecycle management of Le Moyne’s academic software, including evaluation, testing, virtualization, distribution, and support across Windows, Apple Mac OS, Google Chromebook and Apple iOS devices. Utilizes established tools to manage the virtualization and distribution of assigned applications. Routinely audits the application portfolio to identify underutilized software for removal, and monitors applications for software updates. Establishes documentation surrounding application management and practices. Serves as a consultant regarding questions involving software installation, configuration, and maintenance. Student Management Serve as primary professional staff member responsible for hiring, training, mentoring, and supervising approximately 10 student staff. Assist in the development of a comprehensive training program to educate Systems and Network Services student staff. Approves timesheets and absences for direct report(s) using the established systems. Schedules appropriate student staffing to support SNS team needs. General Duties At all times, applies principles and practices that promote the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of Le Moyne’s information and information and technology services. Supports the resolution of technology issues. Ensures that assigned incidents and requests are responded to and resolved in accordance with established standards. Collaborates on the maintenance and renewal of systems and software configuration management tools. Collaborates with other IT staff and Le Moyne community members on assigned projects. Communicates effectively in visual, oral, and written form with key constituencies. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Maintains a constituent centric approach at all times. Demonstrates professionalism in contacts with others. Engages in on-call and weekend support. Job expectations for all Le Moyne College employees: Demonstrates and role-models all of Le Moyne’s mission-based competencies (collaboration, communication, diversity, integrity, leadership and service) in every interaction with all community members and external parties. Strengthen digital literacy skills through education and the application of digital technologies in order to effectively engage in information gathering, utilization and data management while promoting a security culture. Supports cura personalis by treating all individuals with dignity, professionalism and kindness. Promotes cura apostolica by aligning professional goals, objectives, and performance with college’s strategic goals. Demonstrates excellent work attendance, reliability and work ethic. Attends and actively participates in required meetings and training sessions. Complies and adheres to all of Le Moyne’s established policies, procedures and codes of conduct at all times, including all health and safety requirements and regulations, to promote desired behavior and build awareness. Must complete all required federal, state, institution and department trainings. Engages in a planned program of professional development. Continually maintains skills and knowledge relative to the position and technology industry including best practice, evolving operational requirements, and industry trends. Performs a variety of related duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s degree or equivalent academic preparation from a regionally accredited college. 1-3 years of relevant experience supporting desktop, software, and mobile computing systems. Successful, prior supervisory and/or team leadership experience in a professional work environment. Proficiency in Microsoft Windows 11, Active Directory, Group Policy, Windows registry, Windows File and Print Services Working experience with Windows server operating systems Proficiency in GSuite, Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Cloud, and similar productivity tools. Experience in application distribution and virtualization platforms such as AppsAnywhere (or similar management tool) to provide software access. Hands-on experience in configuring SCCM (or similar configuration management tool) to build, deploy and manage PC images Hands-on experience with Jamf (or similar configuration management tool) to build, deploy and manage Mac OS images Experience supporting virtual desktop technologies. Familiar with ITIL (or related) service management practices including incident, problem, configuration, and change management Superior commitment to serving others with empathy, timeliness, accuracy, thoroughness, and professionalism Creative and critical thinker with an open and collaborative style that engenders trust from the College community. Outstanding interpersonal and communication skills; works effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Self-motivated and proactive; works effectively with limited oversight and direction; attentive to detail; organized; ably manages resources, constituencies, projects of varying size, and multiple and competing priorities and deadlines Familiarity with the academic and administrative functions of a college is desirable. TECHNICAL ENVIRONMENT Windows 11, Active Directory, Group Policy, Windows Registry, Window File and Print Apple MacOS and iOS VMware Horizon View, vCenter Google GSuite for EDU, ChromeOS Microsoft SCCM, InTune Microsoft Office, Adobe Creative Suite Software2 AppsAnywhere Desktop Firewall, Anti-Malware Powershell Additional Information: Le Moyne Benefits 403(b) Retirement contribution- (9.5% Employer match) Generous tuition coverage Health insurance options- (Medical, Dental, Vision, Flexible Spending Accounts) Health Savings Accounts- (Partially Employer funded)  Basic Life & AD&D Insurance- (Employer paid) Short and Long Term Disability Insurance (Employer paid) Supplemental Life & AD&D Insurance Voluntary benefits- (Legal, Critical Illness, Hospital Indemnity, Accident Insurance, Pet Insurance etc.) 12 paid holidays Generous time off package  Pay Range: $25.50 - $27.00 per hour Equal Employment Opportunity Le Moyne College prohibits discrimination and harassment of any kind based on race, color, sex, religion, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, genetic information, pregnancy, citizenship & immigration or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws. This policy applies to all employment practices within our organization, including hiring, recruiting, promotion, termination, layoff, recall, leave of absence, compensation, benefits, training, and apprenticeship.  Le Moyne makes hiring decisions based solely on qualifications, merit, and business needs at the time.  Application Instructions: To apply for this position please click the 'Apply Now' button and submit the required materials for consideration: * Cover letter outlining your interest in the position * Current resume * Contact information for 3 professional references"
